  "data/ingredients/unmapped/CMC_PY_Horse_Serum.yaml": {
    "sha256": "39e3ff65e31ecd99696afd0b2d3429fba96751361b019a92933e136372b74077",
    "raw_text": "identifier: UNMAPPED_0740\npreferred_term: CMC + PY + Horse Serum\nsynonyms:\n- synonym_text: CMC + PY + Horse Serum\n  synonym_type: RAW_TEXT\n  source: microbedecoder\nmapping_status: AMBIGUOUS\noccurrence_statistics:\n  total_occurrences: 0\n  media_count: 0\n  source_occurrences:\n  - source: microbedecoder\n    count: 1\n    source_columns: bergey:substrates\ncuration_history:\n- timestamp: '2026-08-04T02:54:09.684805+00:00'\n  curator: audit_import_ingredients[microbedecoder]\n  action: CREATED_AS_UNMAPPED\n  changes: Imported from microbedecoder (source_id=kgmicrobe.compound:cmc_py_horse_serum);\n    no CAS-RN or CHEBI/NCIT match. Curator review needed.\n  new_status: UNMAPPED\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-08-05T00:01:30.894952+00:00'\n  curator: microbedecoder-residual-dispositions\n  action: FLAGGED_NEEDS_EXPERT\n  changes: 'Not a single-compound grounding target: multi-component blend or named\n    medium; no single ontology term grounds it -- needs decomposition into constituents.'\n  previous_status: UNMAPPED\n  new_status: NEEDS_EXPERT\n  llm_assisted: true\n- timestamp: '2026-08-06T00:00:00+00:00'\n  curator: edison_literature_identity\n  action: ANNOTATED\n  changes: 'Edison LITERATURE (PaperQA3) identity research; report at research/ingredients/CMC_PY_Horse_Serum-edison-literature.md\n    (local artifact \u2014 research/ is gitignored, so the findings are quoted here rather\n    than linked). Report verdict: **Recommended interpretation:** a **composite culture-medium\n    recipe shorthand**, not a single chemical, salt/hydrate, commercial product, or\n    uniquely defined named medium. The most defensible decomposition is: CURIEs discussed:\n    UBERON:0001977. Recorded as provenance only \u2014 no grounding applied from this run.\n    Edison''s recommendations are deliberately conservative, and a plausible identifier\n    promoted by a mechanism that never decided anything is what #203 and #263 exist\n    to undo. Any CURIE above is a curator''s to accept or reject.'\n  llm_assisted: true\n- timestamp: '2026-08-14T00:00:00+00:00'\n  curator: decompose_substrate_combinations\n  action: DECOMPOSED_TO_COMPONENTS\n  previous_status: NEEDS_EXPERT\n  new_status: MAPPED\n  changes: 'UNMAPPED_0740 -> kgmicrobe.ingredient:cmc_py_horse_serum (FALLBACK_REGISTRY).\n    The label enumerates its own constituents, so this is a decomposition rather than\n    a mapping: no ontology has a term for ''CMC + PY + Horse Serum'', and none could\n    \u2014 a combination is not a substance. Minted under the #288 STOCK_SOLUTION convention\n    and split on ''+'', which transcribes the label rather than inferring anything.\n    2 of 3 constituents resolve to existing MIM records via docs/data/label_index.csv;\n    PY carries no component_id because MIM has no record for it. ingredient_type=UNDEFINED_MIXTURE\n    because at least one constituent is itself an undefined preparation. No concentrations\n    are recorded: the label states none.'\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-08-14T00:00:00+00:00'\n  curator: apply_curated_decompositions\n  action: REPLACED_COMPONENTS_WITH_CURATED\n  changes: 'components replaced with the curated research decomposition, superseding\n    the label split. Components taken from the curated microbedecoder research decomposition\n    (mappings/microbedecoder_residual_research_decomposition.tsv, strategy=split):\n    the label names its constituents. 4 constituent(s), 4 carrying an identifier.\n    That file was produced by the research pass and never written into the records;\n    this applies it. It resolves constituents a label split cannot \u2014 abbreviations\n    such as PY, and named media such as BHI, state no composition to split on. ingredient_type=UNDEFINED_MIXTURE.\n    No concentrations are recorded: the curated row states none.'\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-08-15T00:00:00+00:00'\n  curator: move_mapped_out_of_unmapped_collection\n  action: MOVED_TO_MAPPED_COLLECTION\n  changes: Moved from unmapped_ingredients.yaml to mapped_ingredients.yaml (#370).\n    The record was already MAPPED; it had been promoted in place by a path that does\n    not move between collections, and reconcile_sssom reads only the mapped collection\n    \u2014 so its mapping was curated but unpublished.\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-08-24T00:00:00+00:00'\n  curator: migrate_component_partonomy\n  action: TYPED_COMPONENT_PARTONOMY\n  changes: '#369: added method/evidence/completeness and explicit reference scope\n    to 4 existing component(s) (EXTERNAL_TERM, MIM_CATALOG); constituent names, identifiers,\n    and concentrations were not changed.'\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-09-21T00:00:00+00:00'\n  curator: mim-semantic-evidence-review\n  action: CORRECTED\n  changes: '#710: original species-description evidence disproves carboxymethylcellulose\n    expansion and a single CMC/PY/serum mixture. Withdrew all four invented component\n    edges and fallback identity, restored UNMAPPED_0740, marked AMBIGUOUS and moved\n    to unmapped. Kept original raw label; full withdrawn claims and prior source record\n    are preserved in reports/semantic_review_20260921/resolution/components/before-records.json.'\n  previous_status: MAPPED\n  new_status: AMBIGUOUS\n  llm_assisted: true\nnotes: MicrobeDecoder flattened separate Filifactor villosus culture contexts into\n  CMC + PY + Horse Serum. Love et al. 1979 (doi:10.1099/00207713-29-3-241) describes\n  cooked meat-carbohydrate and peptone-yeast extract cultures supplemented with horse\n  serum. CMC is not carboxymethylcellulose here. This source expression is retained\n  as AMBIGUOUS until separate source preparations are represented; it has no asserted\n  single-mixture components or ontology identity.\n"
  },
