  "data/ingredients/mapped/Sodium_Acetate3h2o.yaml": {
    "sha256": "81d6967da5cca894d87f94c503bd553d581b146f141c47a6a064caa6365a705b",
    "raw_text": "identifier: CHEBI:32138\npreferred_term: Sodium acetate\u00b73H2O\nontology_mapping:\n  ontology_id: CHEBI:32138\n  ontology_label: sodium acetate trihydrate\n  ontology_source: CHEBI\n  mapping_quality: NARROW_MATCH\n  evidence:\n  - evidence_type: DATABASE_MATCH\n    source: CultureMech\n    notes: '[HISTORICAL \u2014 superseded by the #321 re-grade below: this record is a\n      hydrate of CHEBI:32954, not an exact match to it] Imported from CultureMech\n      pipeline, quality=DIRECT_MATCH'\n  - evidence_type: DATABASE_MATCH\n    source: MIM curation (#321/#334)\n    notes: identifier CHEBI:32954 -> kgmicrobe.compound:sodium_acetate3h2o; mapping_quality\n      SYNONYM_MATCH -> NARROW_MATCH. The record is a hydrate of CHEBI:32954 ('sodium\n      acetate') and was sharing that term's identifier \u2014 the identity collapse MAPPING_SEMANTICS\n      \u00a73 forbids, which made a distinct substance indistinguishable from its anhydrous\n      parent downstream. ChEBI has no term for this hydrate and the record carries\n      no verified CAS, so steps 1 and 2 are unavailable and step 3 applies.\n  - evidence_type: DATABASE_MATCH\n    source: MIM curation (#321)\n    notes: molecular_formula 'C2H3O2.Na' -> 'C2H3O2.Na.3H2O'. The recorded value described\n      the anhydrous salt while the label names a hydrate, understating the mass by\n      18 g/mol per water. Corrected because the label states 3 water(s) of hydration,\n      and the recorded formula was byte-identical to the anhydrous parent CHEBI:32954's\n      ChEBI formula ('C2H3O2.Na') \u2014 the mark of a value inherited from the parent\n      rather than measured for this record. Water appended in ChEBI's own dot-separated\n      notation.\nsynonyms:\n- synonym_text: 'Role: Buffer; Properties: Defined component, Organic compound, Simple\n    component'\n  synonym_type: RAW_TEXT\n  source: CultureMech\n- synonym_text: 'Role: Buffer; Properties: Organic compound, Simple component, Defined\n    component'\n  synonym_type: RAW_TEXT\n  source: CultureMech\n- synonym_text: Sodium acetate\u30fb3H2O\n  synonym_type: HYDRATE_FORM\n  source: kg_microbe\n- synonym_text: anhydrous sodium acetate\n  synonym_type: EXACT_SYNONYM\n  source: kg_microbe\n- synonym_text: sodium acetate anhydrous\n  synonym_type: EXACT_SYNONYM\n  source: kg_microbe\nmapping_status: REJECTED\noccurrence_statistics:\n  total_occurrences: 0\n  media_count: 0\ncuration_history:\n- timestamp: '2026-03-09T06:54:18.022301+00:00'\n  curator: import_from_culturemech\n  action: IMPORTED\n  changes: Initial import from CultureMech pipeline\n  new_status: MAPPED\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-04-05T21:48:45.714031+00:00'\n  curator: fetch_cas_rn_from_culturebot_csv\n  action: ADDED_CAS_RN\n  changes: 'Added CAS-RN:127-09-3 from CultureBotHT compounds_to_cas.csv (matched:\n    Sodium acetate\u00b73H2O)'\n  new_status: MAPPED\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-04-18T00:00:00+00:00'\n  curator: cbclaw_kg_microbe_sweep\n  action: ADDED_SYNONYMS\n  changes: 'Added 3 synonyms from kg-microbe P4.4 enrichment: Sodium acetate\u30fb3H2O,\n    anhydrous sodium acetate, sodium acetate anhydrous'\n  new_status: MAPPED\n  llm_assisted: true\n- timestamp: '2026-05-01T07:35:36.202533+00:00'\n  curator: auto_classify_ingredient_type\n  action: AUTO_CLASSIFY_INGREDIENT_TYPE\n  changes: set ingredient_type=SINGLE_INGREDIENT (CHEBI primary)\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-05-01T08:08:32.290584+00:00'\n  curator: auto_classify_ingredient_type\n  action: AUTO_BACKFILL_CHEBI_CHEMISTRY\n  changes: molecular_formula=C2H3O2.Na; inchi=InChI=1S/C2H4O2.Na/c1-2(3)4;/h1H3,(H,3,4);/q;+1/p-;\n    smiles=CC(=O)[O-].[Na+]\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-05-02T03:12:18.299629+00:00'\n  curator: auto_classify_ingredient_type\n  action: AUTO_CLASSIFY_INGREDIENT_TYPE\n  changes: set ingredient_type=SINGLE_INGREDIENT (chemical structure populated (molecular_formula))\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-05-29T23:35:36.112790+00:00'\n  curator: extract_roles_from_synonyms\n  action: ANNOTATED\n  changes: 'Added media role: BUFFER (confidence: 1.00)'\n- timestamp: '2026-07-20T00:00:00+00:00'\n  curator: migrate_media_roles_to_facets\n  action: ANNOTATED\n  changes: 'Migrated legacy media_roles to role facets (#128): BUFFER -> physicochemical_roles.BUFFER'\n- timestamp: '2026-08-10T00:00:00+00:00'\n  curator: regrade_synonym_matches\n  action: REGRADED_EXACT_TO_SYNONYM\n  changes: mapping_quality EXACT_MATCH -> SYNONYM_MATCH (#317). The record's label\n    does not equal the term's primary label 'sodium acetate'; it matches the ChEBI\n    synonym 'anhydrous sodium acetate' on CHEBI:32954. The schema defines EXACT_MATCH\n    as a direct match to the term and SYNONYM_MATCH as a match to a known synonym,\n    so the recorded grade overstated. ontology_id is unchanged \u2014 the term is correct.\n    The SSSOM predicate is unaffected (both grades emit skos:exactMatch).\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-08-13T00:00:00+00:00'\n  curator: mint_hydrate_registry_terms\n  action: MINTED_REGISTRY_FOR_HYDRATE\n  changes: identifier CHEBI:32954 -> kgmicrobe.compound:sodium_acetate3h2o; mapping_quality\n    SYNONYM_MATCH -> NARROW_MATCH (#321/#334); \u00a73 step 3.\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-08-13T00:00:00+00:00'\n  curator: add_water_of_hydration\n  action: ADDED_WATER_OF_HYDRATION\n  changes: molecular_formula 'C2H3O2.Na' -> 'C2H3O2.Na.3H2O' (#321); the label states\n    3 water(s) of hydration, and the recorded formula was byte-identical to the anhydrous\n    parent CHEBI:32954's ChEBI formula ('C2H3O2.Na') \u2014 the mark of a value inherited\n    from the parent rather than measured for this record. Water appended in ChEBI's\n    own dot-separated notation.\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-08-13T00:00:00+00:00'\n  curator: merge_minted_hydrate_duplicates\n  action: MERGED_INTO\n  changes: 'Merged into CHEBI:32138 ''Sodium acetate trihydrate''; occurrences transferred.\n    The ''kgmicrobe.compound:sodium_acetate3h2o'' minted for this record is withdrawn:\n    \u00a73 step 3 requires that no specific term exists, and one does (ChEBI label search\n    for the trihydrate of the minted-off parent), so step 1 applied and the target\n    identifier was already held. Tombstoned REJECTED, SSSOM rows dropped (#321).'\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-08-15T00:00:00+00:00'\n  curator: fix_tombstone_pointers\n  action: REFRESHED_TOMBSTONE_ONTOLOGY_ID\n  changes: 'ontology_id CHEBI:32954 -> CHEBI:32138 (#360). The merge set identifier\n    and status but left ontology_mapping untouched, so this tombstone kept advertising\n    a term it no longer asserts \u2014 anything indexing by ontology_id routed through\n    it. Now agrees with the merge target ''Sodium acetate trihydrate''. Provenance\n    is unaffected: what the record used to assert is in this history.'\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-09-09T00:00:00+00:00'\n  curator: fix_kg_microbe_node_id_drift\n  action: CORRECTED\n  changes: kg_microbe_node_id CHEBI:32954 -> CHEBI:32138 (#554). The compatibility\n    node id lagged a same-prefix identifier correction; the downstream node id must\n    match the curated identifier unless a record intentionally crosses CURIE prefixes.\n  llm_assisted: false\nchemical_properties:\n  cas_rn: 127-09-3\n  data_source: CultureBotHT compounds_to_cas.csv\n  retrieval_date: '2026-04-05T21:48:45.714029+00:00'\n  molecular_formula: C2H3O2.Na.3H2O\n  inchi: InChI=1S/C2H4O2.Na/c1-2(3)4;/h1H3,(H,3,4);/q;+1/p-1\n  smiles: CC(=O)[O-].[Na+]\nkg_microbe_node_id: CHEBI:32138\ningredient_type: SINGLE_INGREDIENT\nphysicochemical_roles:\n- role: BUFFER\n  confidence: 1.0\n  evidence:\n  - reference_text: CultureMech database (2 occurrences as 'Buffer')\n    reference_type: DATABASE_ENTRY\n    url: https://github.com/CultureBotAI/CultureMech\n    excerpt: 'Role: Buffer; Properties: Defined component, Organic compound, Simple\n      component'\n    curator_note: Widespread use in media formulations (2 occurrences). High confidence\n      based on 'Defined component' property.\n"
  },
