    "raw_text": "identifier: CHEBI:64758\npreferred_term: Na2-EDTA x 2 H2O\nontology_mapping:\n  ontology_id: CHEBI:64758\n  ontology_label: EDTA disodium salt dihydrate\n  ontology_source: CHEBI\n  mapping_quality: NARROW_MATCH\n  evidence:\n  - evidence_type: DATABASE_MATCH\n    source: CultureMech\n    notes: '[HISTORICAL \u2014 superseded by the #321 re-grade below: this record is a\n      hydrate of CHEBI:64734, not an exact match to it] Imported from CultureMech\n      pipeline, quality=DIRECT_MATCH'\n  - evidence_type: DATABASE_MATCH\n    source: MIM curation (#321/#334)\n    notes: identifier CHEBI:64734 -> kgmicrobe.compound:na2-edta_x_2_h2o; mapping_quality\n      EXACT_MATCH -> NARROW_MATCH. The record is a hydrate of CHEBI:64734 ('EDTA disodium\n      salt (anhydrous)') and was sharing that term's identifier \u2014 the identity collapse\n      MAPPING_SEMANTICS \u00a73 forbids, which made a distinct substance indistinguishable\n      from its anhydrous parent downstream. ChEBI has no term for this hydrate and\n      the record carries no verified CAS, so steps 1 and 2 are unavailable and step\n      3 applies.\n  - evidence_type: DATABASE_MATCH\n    source: MIM curation (#321)\n    notes: molecular_formula 'C10H14N2O8.2Na' -> 'C10H14N2O8.2Na.2H2O'. The recorded\n      value described the anhydrous salt while the label names a hydrate, understating\n      the mass by 18 g/mol per water. Corrected because the label states 2 water(s)\n      of hydration, and the recorded formula was byte-identical to the anhydrous parent\n      CHEBI:64734's ChEBI formula ('C10H14N2O8.2Na') \u2014 the mark of a value inherited\n      from the parent rather than measured for this record. Water appended in ChEBI's\n      own dot-separated notation.\nsynonyms:\n- synonym_text: 'Properties: Defined component, Organic compound, Simple component'\n  synonym_type: RAW_TEXT\n  source: CultureMech\n- synonym_text: 'Properties: Defined component, Simple component, Organic compound'\n  synonym_type: RAW_TEXT\n  source: CultureMech\n- synonym_text: EDTA disodium (anhydrous)\n  synonym_type: REJECTED_LABEL\n  source: kg_microbe\n- synonym_text: EDTA disodium salt (anhydrous)\n  synonym_type: REJECTED_LABEL\n  source: kg_microbe\n- synonym_text: Edetate disodium anhydrous\n  synonym_type: REJECTED_LABEL\n  source: kg_microbe\n- synonym_text: Na-EDTA x 2 H2O\n  synonym_type: HYDRATE_FORM\n  source: kg_microbe\n- synonym_text: Na2-EDTA\u00b72H2O\n  synonym_type: HYDRATE_FORM\n  source: kg_microbe_via_hydration_routing\n- synonym_text: 'Properties: Simple component, Organic compound, Defined component'\n  synonym_type: RAW_TEXT\n  source: CultureMech\n- synonym_text: disodium 2,2',2'',2'''-(ethane-1,2-diyldiammonio)tetraacetate\n  synonym_type: REJECTED_LABEL\n  source: chebi_synonym_review\nmapping_status: REJECTED\noccurrence_statistics:\n  total_occurrences: 0\n  media_count: 0\ncuration_history:\n- timestamp: '2026-03-09T06:54:18.022301+00:00'\n  curator: import_from_culturemech\n  action: IMPORTED\n  changes: Initial import from CultureMech pipeline\n  new_status: MAPPED\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-04-05T23:45:36.103846+00:00'\n  curator: fetch_cas_rn_with_preprocessing\n  action: ADDED_CAS_RN\n  changes: Added CAS-RN:7487-55-0 from PubChem API (preprocessed) via name preprocessing\n    (Na-EDTA x 2 H2O)\n  new_status: MAPPED\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-04-05T23:45:45.687273+00:00'\n  curator: fetch_cas_rn_with_preprocessing\n  action: ADDED_CAS_RN\n  changes: Added CAS-RN:7487-55-0 from PubChem API (preprocessed) via name preprocessing\n    (Na2-EDTA x 2 H2O)\n  new_status: MAPPED\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-04-18T00:00:00+00:00'\n  curator: cbclaw_kg_microbe_sweep\n  action: ADDED_SYNONYMS\n  changes: 'Added 4 synonyms from kg-microbe P4.4 enrichment: EDTA disodium (anhydrous),\n    EDTA disodium salt (anhydrous), Edetate disodium anhydrous, Na-EDTA x 2 H2O'\n  new_status: MAPPED\n  llm_assisted: true\n- timestamp: '2026-04-18T00:00:00+00:00'\n  curator: cbclaw_kg_microbe_sweep\n  action: ADDED_SYNONYMS\n  changes: 'Added 3 synonyms from kg-microbe P4.4 enrichment: EDTA disodium (anhydrous),\n    EDTA disodium salt (anhydrous), Edetate disodium anhydrous'\n  new_status: MAPPED\n  llm_assisted: true\n- timestamp: '2026-04-19T06:30:07.230267+00:00'\n  curator: audit_p44_hydration_routing\n  action: ADDED_SYNONYMS_VIA_HYDRATION_ROUTING\n  changes: 'Added 1 synonyms re-routed from anhydrous/hydrate sibling records (Na2-edta.yaml):\n    Na2-EDTA\u00b72H2O'\n  new_status: MAPPED\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-04-19T07:23:20.785693+00:00'\n  curator: audit_mim_merge\n  action: MERGED_FROM_DUPLICATES\n  changes: 'Absorbed 1 duplicate MIM record(s) into this one: Na-edta_X_2_H2o.yaml.\n    Synonyms, curation_history, and occurrence counts were unioned/summed; winner\n    selected by highest occurrence count with preferred_term readability tie-break.'\n  new_status: MAPPED\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-05-01T07:35:35.098427+00:00'\n  curator: auto_classify_ingredient_type\n  action: AUTO_CLASSIFY_INGREDIENT_TYPE\n  changes: set ingredient_type=SINGLE_INGREDIENT (CHEBI primary)\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-05-01T08:08:31.163989+00:00'\n  curator: auto_classify_ingredient_type\n  action: AUTO_BACKFILL_CHEBI_CHEMISTRY\n  changes: molecular_formula=C10H14N2O8.2Na; inchi=InChI=1S/C10H16N2O8.2Na/c13-7(14)3-11(4-8(15)16)1-;\n    smiles=O=C([O-])C[NH+](CC[NH+](CC(=O)[O-])CC(=O)[O-])CC(=\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-05-02T03:12:16.894725+00:00'\n  curator: auto_classify_ingredient_type\n  action: AUTO_CLASSIFY_INGREDIENT_TYPE\n  changes: set ingredient_type=SINGLE_INGREDIENT (chemical structure populated (molecular_formula))\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-06-02T07:05:13.391811+00:00'\n  curator: infer_roles_from_name_lists\n  action: ANNOTATED\n  changes: 'Added media role: CHELATOR (confidence: 0.80)'\n- timestamp: '2026-06-09T05:23:46.805298+00:00'\n  curator: correct_stale_ontology_labels.py\n  action: CORRECTED\n  changes: 'ontology_label ''Na2-EDTA x 2 H2O'' -> ''EDTA disodium salt (anhydrous)'':\n    synced to canonical CHEBI label (preferred_term ''Na2-EDTA x 2 H2O'' unchanged).'\n- timestamp: '2026-07-20T00:00:00+00:00'\n  curator: migrate_media_roles_to_facets\n  action: ANNOTATED\n  changes: 'Migrated legacy media_roles to role facets (#128): CHELATOR -> physicochemical_roles.CHELATOR'\n- timestamp: '2026-08-13T00:00:00+00:00'\n  curator: mint_hydrate_registry_terms\n  action: MINTED_REGISTRY_FOR_HYDRATE\n  changes: identifier CHEBI:64734 -> kgmicrobe.compound:na2-edta_x_2_h2o; mapping_quality\n    EXACT_MATCH -> NARROW_MATCH (#321/#334); \u00a73 step 3.\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-08-13T00:00:00+00:00'\n  curator: add_water_of_hydration\n  action: ADDED_WATER_OF_HYDRATION\n  changes: molecular_formula 'C10H14N2O8.2Na' -> 'C10H14N2O8.2Na.2H2O' (#321); the\n    label states 2 water(s) of hydration, and the recorded formula was byte-identical\n    to the anhydrous parent CHEBI:64734's ChEBI formula ('C10H14N2O8.2Na') \u2014 the mark\n    of a value inherited from the parent rather than measured for this record. Water\n    appended in ChEBI's own dot-separated notation.\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-08-13T00:00:00+00:00'\n  curator: merge_minted_hydrate_duplicates\n  action: MERGED_INTO\n  changes: 'Merged into CHEBI:64758 ''Na2EDTA\u00b72H2O''; occurrences transferred. The\n    ''kgmicrobe.compound:na2-edta_x_2_h2o'' minted for this record is withdrawn: \u00a73\n    step 3 requires that no specific term exists, and one does (ChEBI label search\n    for the dihydrate of the minted-off parent), so step 1 applied and the target\n    identifier was already held. Tombstoned REJECTED, SSSOM rows dropped (#321).'\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-08-15T00:00:00+00:00'\n  curator: fix_tombstone_pointers\n  action: REFRESHED_TOMBSTONE_ONTOLOGY_ID\n  changes: 'ontology_id CHEBI:64734 -> CHEBI:64758 (#360). The merge set identifier\n    and status but left ontology_mapping untouched, so this tombstone kept advertising\n    a term it no longer asserts \u2014 anything indexing by ontology_id routed through\n    it. Now agrees with the merge target ''Na2EDTA\u00b72H2O''. Provenance is unaffected:\n    what the record used to assert is in this history.'\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-09-09T00:00:00+00:00'\n  curator: fix_kg_microbe_node_id_drift\n  action: CORRECTED\n  changes: kg_microbe_node_id CHEBI:64734 -> CHEBI:64758 (#554). The compatibility\n    node id lagged a same-prefix identifier correction; the downstream node id must\n    match the curated identifier unless a record intentionally crosses CURIE prefixes.\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-09-22T20:41:14.285965+00:00'\n  curator: claude\n  action: REJECTED_PARENT_NAME_SYNONYMS\n  changes: 'Retyped names of the parent compound or of a different hydrate as provenance-only\n    REJECTED_LABEL, because this record is a distinct salt, hydrate or tombstone form\n    and the label index resolved the parent''s name here (#232): ''EDTA disodium (anhydrous)'';\n    ''EDTA disodium salt (anhydrous)''; ''Edetate disodium anhydrous''; \"disodium\n    2,2'',2'''',2''''''-(ethane-1,2-diyldiammonio)tetraacetate\". Preserved original\n    text and source metadata. No identity, mapping, role, or remaining-synonym claim\n    was adjudicated.'\n  llm_assisted: true\nchemical_properties:\n  cas_rn: 7487-55-0\n  data_source: PubChem API (preprocessed)\n  retrieval_date: '2026-04-05T23:45:45.687263+00:00'\n  molecular_formula: C10H14N2O8.2Na.2H2O\n  inchi: InChI=1S/C10H16N2O8.2Na/c13-7(14)3-11(4-8(15)16)1-2-12(5-9(17)18)6-10(19)20;;/h1-6H2,(H,13,14)(H,15,16)(H,17,18)(H,19,20);;/q;2*+1/p-2\n  smiles: O=C([O-])C[NH+](CC[NH+](CC(=O)[O-])CC(=O)[O-])CC(=O)[O-].[Na+].[Na+]\nkg_microbe_node_id: CHEBI:64758\ningredient_type: SINGLE_INGREDIENT\nphysicochemical_roles:\n- role: CHELATOR\n  confidence: 0.8\n  evidence:\n  - reference_type: COMPUTATIONAL_PREDICTION\n    reference_text: Inferred from curated media-role name pattern\n    curator_note: Provisional role from a curated name-pattern rule; review recommended.\n"
