  "data/ingredients/mapped/Cadmium_Acetate_Dihydrate.yaml": {
    "sha256": "1769c867fc43e18416a493889e69d0b6537ab07509bf0e81cfb5cb87bc587310",
    "raw_text": "identifier: cas:5743-04-4\npreferred_term: Cadmium acetate dihydrate\nontology_mapping:\n  ontology_id: CHEBI:232796\n  ontology_label: cadmium acetate\n  ontology_source: CHEBI\n  mapping_quality: NARROW_MATCH\n  evidence:\n  - evidence_type: DATABASE_MATCH\n    source: CultureBotHT\n    notes: 'Imported from CultureBotHT. CAS-RN 5743-04-4 present, but no CHEBI entry\n      exists (checked OAK CHEBI sqlite + PubChem CID synonyms). Used in 1 CultureBot\n      media; samples: FW104 COMM. Curator can promote to a CHEBI primary if/when CHEBI\n      adds the term.'\n  - evidence_type: DATABASE_MATCH\n    source: CHEBI via PubChem (pubchem-xref)\n    notes: Parent class identified via pubchem-xref; matched_via='pubchem CID 10986'\n  - evidence_type: DATABASE_MATCH\n    source: MIM curation (#342)\n    notes: 'mapping_quality NARROW_MATCH -> CLOSE_MATCH, predicate skos:narrowMatch\n      -> skos:closeMatch. narrowMatch asserts this record is *narrower in meaning*\n      than CHEBI:232796 (''cadmium acetate'') \u2014 a subsumption ChEBI itself denies:\n      it files hydrates under CHEBI:35505 ''hydrate'', never under the anhydrous compound,\n      which is not an ancestor even transitively. A hydrate is a distinct substance\n      containing the anhydrous form, not a specialization of it. closeMatch claims\n      similarity without subsumption. The ontology_id and the record''s own identifier\n      are unchanged.'\n  - evidence_type: DATABASE_MATCH\n    source: MIM curation (#321)\n    notes: molecular_formula 'C4H6CdO4' -> 'C4H6CdO4.2H2O'. The recorded value described\n      the anhydrous salt while the label names a hydrate, understating the mass by\n      18 g/mol per water. Corrected because the label states 2 water(s) of hydration,\n      and the recorded formula was byte-identical to the anhydrous parent CHEBI:232796's\n      ChEBI formula ('2C2H3O2.Cd') \u2014 the mark of a value inherited from the parent\n      rather than measured for this record. Water appended in ChEBI's own dot-separated\n      notation.\n  - evidence_type: MANUAL_CURATION\n    source: MIM Step7d scientific review (#901)\n    notes: 'Source CAS5743-04-4 plus supplier/PubChem confirms cadmium acetate dihydrate;\n      keep own CAS distinct from CHEBI232796 dry parent. Change quality to NARROW_MATCH/broadMatch\n      to232796; no exact dry-parent identity. Retain C4H6CdO4.2H2O and CAS. Withdraw\n      dry SMILES, dry InChI and CID10986; fresh dihydrate CID6537495 demonstrates\n      the mismatch but is not automatically imported as replacement. Primary source\n      references: https://www.sigmaaldrich.com/US/en/product/mm/102003; https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/rest/pug/compound/name/5743-04-4/property/Title,MolecularFormula,MolecularWeight,InChI,InChIKey,CanonicalSMILES/JSON;\n      https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/backend/api/public/compound/232796/. Captures, exact\n      input hashes and scope limits: reports/step7d_mapping_901_20261103/evidence-manifest.json.\n      Independent review identifies the existing exact synonym ''cadmium(2+);diacetate''\n      as the water-free parent, not this hydrate; preserve it as REJECTED_LABEL. This\n      curation adds no scientific, mapping-release or role approval; changed owner\n      bytes withdraw inherited support.'\nsynonyms:\n- synonym_text: cadmium(2+);diacetate\n  synonym_type: REJECTED_LABEL\n  source: chebi_synonym_review\nmapping_status: MAPPED\noccurrence_statistics:\n  total_occurrences: 1\n  media_count: 1\ncuration_history:\n- timestamp: '2026-04-29T06:51:33.117170+00:00'\n  curator: audit_add_remaining_culturebotht\n  action: CREATED_FROM_CAS_FALLBACK\n  changes: Created with cas:5743-04-4 as primary identifier; no CHEBI entry exists\n    for this compound.\n  new_status: MAPPED\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-05-01T07:35:32.537438+00:00'\n  curator: auto_classify_ingredient_type\n  action: AUTO_CLASSIFY_INGREDIENT_TYPE\n  changes: 'set ingredient_type=SINGLE_INGREDIENT (cas: primary (defined chemical))'\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-05-02T02:52:12.066648+00:00'\n  curator: auto_classify_ingredient_type\n  action: AUTO_BACKFILL_PUBCHEM_CHEMISTRY\n  changes: molecular_formula=C4H6CdO4; smiles=CC(=O)[O-].CC(=O)[O-].[Cd+2]; inchi=InChI=1S/2C2H4O2.Cd/c2*1-2(3)4;/h2*1H3,(H,3,4);/q;\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-05-02T03:12:13.002184+00:00'\n  curator: auto_classify_ingredient_type\n  action: AUTO_CLASSIFY_INGREDIENT_TYPE\n  changes: set ingredient_type=SINGLE_INGREDIENT (chemical structure populated (molecular_formula))\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-05-02T04:42:29.212932+00:00'\n  curator: backfill_parent_terms\n  action: BACKFILL_PARENT_CHEBI\n  changes: set ontology_mapping parent=CHEBI:232796 (pubchem-xref)\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-08-13T00:00:00+00:00'\n  curator: regrade_hydrate_to_close_match\n  action: REGRADED_HYDRATE_TO_CLOSE_MATCH\n  changes: mapping_quality NARROW_MATCH -> CLOSE_MATCH (#342); a hydrate is not subsumed\n    by its anhydrous form, and ChEBI does not model it as such.\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-08-13T00:00:00+00:00'\n  curator: add_water_of_hydration\n  action: ADDED_WATER_OF_HYDRATION\n  changes: molecular_formula 'C4H6CdO4' -> 'C4H6CdO4.2H2O' (#321); the label states\n    2 water(s) of hydration, and the recorded formula was byte-identical to the anhydrous\n    parent CHEBI:232796's ChEBI formula ('2C2H3O2.Cd') \u2014 the mark of a value inherited\n    from the parent rather than measured for this record. Water appended in ChEBI's\n    own dot-separated notation.\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-11-03T06:07:03.766598+00:00'\n  curator: claude\n  action: CORRECTED\n  changes: 'Step 7d (#901; #1117 where applicable): applied only the reviewed field\n    changes [{\"op\":\"set\",\"path\":[\"ontology_mapping\",\"mapping_quality\"],\"before\":\"CLOSE_MATCH\",\"after\":\"NARROW_MATCH\"},{\"op\":\"remove\",\"path\":[\"chemical_properties\",\"smiles\"],\"before\":\"CC(=O)[O-].CC(=O)[O-].[Cd+2]\",\"after\":null},{\"op\":\"remove\",\"path\":[\"chemical_properties\",\"inchi\"],\"before\":\"InChI=1S/2C2H4O2.Cd/c2*1-2(3)4;/h2*1H3,(H,3,4);/q;;+2/p-2\",\"after\":null},{\"op\":\"remove\",\"path\":[\"chemical_properties\",\"pubchem_cid\"],\"before\":10986,\"after\":null},{\"op\":\"set\",\"path\":[\"synonyms\",0,\"synonym_type\"],\"before\":\"EXACT_SYNONYM\",\"after\":\"REJECTED_LABEL\"}].\n    Original values are preserved here and in the immutable source preimages. Appended\n    scoped mapping evidence. NARROW_MATCH serializes skos:broadMatch; CAS_RN_LOOKUP\n    on the form-specific NCIt identity serializes skos:exactMatch. Preserved prior\n    history, roles, status and occurrence counts; no owner merge or new scientific\n    approval. Review: reports/step7d_mapping_901_20261103/authors/science-a/; primary\n    captures: reports/step7d_mapping_901_20261103/evidence-manifest.json.'\n  previous_status: MAPPED\n  new_status: MAPPED\n  llm_assisted: true\n  llm_model: gpt-6\nchemical_properties:\n  cas_rn: 5743-04-4\n  data_source: CultureBotHT compounds_to_cas.csv\n  retrieval_date: '2026-04-29T06:51:33.117170+00:00'\n  molecular_formula: C4H6CdO4.2H2O\ningredient_type: SINGLE_INGREDIENT\n"
  },
