    "sha256": "a439a3394c28fc8b8d7d93897de2c010cd3ffb2e5a0c67838c7f497fcf0bb413",
    "raw_text": "identifier: kgmicrobe.compound:chlorhexidine_diacetate_salt_hydrate\npreferred_term: Chlorhexidine diacetate salt hydrate\nontology_mapping:\n  ontology_id: CHEBI:81711\n  ontology_label: chlorhexidine acetate\n  ontology_source: CHEBI\n  mapping_quality: NARROW_MATCH\n  evidence:\n  - evidence_type: DATABASE_MATCH\n    source: CultureBotHT\n    notes: 'Imported from CultureBotHT. CAS-RN\u2192CHEBI mapping resolved via OAK CHEBI\n      sqlite (cas xref). FEBA/Hans80 panels: Hans80Anti, Hans80metals.'\n  - evidence_type: DATABASE_MATCH\n    source: MIM curation (#321/#334)\n    notes: identifier CHEBI:81711 -> kgmicrobe.compound:chlorhexidine_diacetate_salt_hydrate;\n      mapping_quality EXACT_MATCH -> NARROW_MATCH. The record is a hydrate of CHEBI:81711\n      ('chlorhexidine acetate') and was sharing that term's identifier \u2014 the identity\n      collapse MAPPING_SEMANTICS \u00a73 forbids, which made a distinct substance indistinguishable\n      from its anhydrous parent downstream. ChEBI has no term for this hydrate and\n      the record carries no verified CAS, so steps 1 and 2 are unavailable and step\n      3 applies.\n  - evidence_type: DATABASE_MATCH\n    source: MIM curation (#342)\n    notes: 'mapping_quality NARROW_MATCH -> CLOSE_MATCH, predicate skos:narrowMatch\n      -> skos:closeMatch. narrowMatch asserts this record is *narrower in meaning*\n      than CHEBI:81711 (''chlorhexidine acetate'') \u2014 a subsumption ChEBI itself denies:\n      it files hydrates under CHEBI:35505 ''hydrate'', never under the anhydrous compound,\n      which is not an ancestor even transitively. A hydrate is a distinct substance\n      containing the anhydrous form, not a specialization of it. closeMatch claims\n      similarity without subsumption. The ontology_id and the record''s own identifier\n      are unchanged.'\n  - evidence_type: MANUAL_CURATION\n    source: MIM Step7d scientific review (#901)\n    notes: 'Historical C6143 and current supplier explicitly identify chlorhexidine\n      diacetate salt hydrate, current formula xH2O. This settles the source-defined\n      variable hydrate, not a fixed monohydrate. Retain its local identity distinct\n      from water-free CHEBI81711. Use NARROW_MATCH/broadMatch to the diacetate parent.\n      Current supplier CAS206986-79-0 yields mixed PubChem forms and does not justify\n      any exact CAS or ontology primary promotion. 7b removed dry structures. Historical\n      chemical CAS56-95-1 is the water-free parent CAS; move procurement context to\n      supplied_form with explicit historical/current disagreement, preserving both\n      observations without exact-identity assertion. Primary source references: https://www.sigmaaldrich.com/US/en/product/sigma/c6143;\n      https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/rest/pug/substance/sourceid/Sigma-Aldrich/C6143_SIGMA/JSON;\n      https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/rest/pug/compound/name/56-95-1/property/Title,MolecularFormula,MolecularWeight,InChI,InChIKey,CanonicalSMILES/JSON;\n      https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/rest/pug/compound/name/206986-79-0/property/Title,MolecularFormula,InChI,InChIKey/JSON;\n      https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/backend/api/public/compound/81711/. Captures, exact\n      input hashes and scope limits: reports/step7d_mapping_901_20261103/evidence-manifest.json.\n      Independent review identifies the existing exact synonym ''N,N''''''''-hexane-1,6-diylbis[N''-(4-chlorophenyl)triimidodicarbonic\n      diamide] acetate (1:2)'' as the water-free parent, not this hydrate; preserve\n      it as REJECTED_LABEL. This curation adds no scientific, mapping-release or role\n      approval; changed owner bytes withdraw inherited support.'\nsynonyms:\n- synonym_text: N,N''''-hexane-1,6-diylbis[N'-(4-chlorophenyl)triimidodicarbonic diamide]\n    acetate (1:2)\n  synonym_type: REJECTED_LABEL\n  source: chebi_synonym_review\nmapping_status: MAPPED\noccurrence_statistics:\n  total_occurrences: 0\n  media_count: 0\ncuration_history:\n- timestamp: '2026-04-29T06:34:31.158938+00:00'\n  curator: audit_cas_chebi_followup\n  action: CREATED_FROM_CAS_LOOKUP\n  changes: 'Created from CultureBotHT CAS-RN=56-95-1; CHEBI resolved via OAK CHEBI\n    sqlite (cas xref); Imported from CultureBotHT. CAS-RN\u2192CHEBI mapping resolved via\n    OAK CHEBI sqlite (cas xref). FEBA/Hans80 panels: Hans80Anti, Hans80metals.'\n  new_status: MAPPED\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-05-01T07:35:32.757606+00:00'\n  curator: auto_classify_ingredient_type\n  action: AUTO_CLASSIFY_INGREDIENT_TYPE\n  changes: set ingredient_type=SINGLE_INGREDIENT (CHEBI primary)\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-05-01T08:08:28.592726+00:00'\n  curator: auto_classify_ingredient_type\n  action: AUTO_BACKFILL_CHEBI_CHEMISTRY\n  changes: molecular_formula=C22H30Cl2N10.2C2H4O2; inchi=InChI=1S/C22H30Cl2N10.2C2H4O2/c23-15-5-9-17(10-6-1;\n    smiles=CC(=O)O.CC(=O)O.N=C(NCCCCCCNC(=N)NC(=N)Nc1ccc(Cl)c\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-05-02T03:12:13.325580+00:00'\n  curator: auto_classify_ingredient_type\n  action: AUTO_CLASSIFY_INGREDIENT_TYPE\n  changes: set ingredient_type=SINGLE_INGREDIENT (chemical structure populated (molecular_formula))\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-08-13T00:00:00+00:00'\n  curator: mint_hydrate_registry_terms\n  action: MINTED_REGISTRY_FOR_HYDRATE\n  changes: identifier CHEBI:81711 -> kgmicrobe.compound:chlorhexidine_diacetate_salt_hydrate;\n    mapping_quality EXACT_MATCH -> NARROW_MATCH (#321/#334); \u00a73 step 3.\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-08-13T00:00:00+00:00'\n  curator: regrade_hydrate_to_close_match\n  action: REGRADED_HYDRATE_TO_CLOSE_MATCH\n  changes: mapping_quality NARROW_MATCH -> CLOSE_MATCH (#342); a hydrate is not subsumed\n    by its anhydrous form, and ChEBI does not model it as such.\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-11-02T05:34:27.474256+00:00'\n  curator: Codex\n  action: CORRECTED_HYDRATE_STOCK_CHEMISTRY\n  changes: '#871/#268 bounded source chemistry correction. Removed fields: chemical_properties.inchi,\n    chemical_properties.smiles, chemical_properties.molecular_formula. Set fields:\n    {}. Whole hydrate has unspecified water content; current unqualified structures/formula\n    exactly match the parent ontology. Sigma C6143 official PDF extraction, primary/web-primary-1.txt\n    No fixed hydration count, new CAS, new formula, supplier assignment or mapping\n    repair. Suppliers sometimes publish dry/anhydrous descriptors for hydrate products;\n    removal concerns unqualified whole-record fields, not a claim the supplier is\n    wrong. C6143 names a hydrate but gives an anhydrous-looking formula without specifying\n    water stoichiometry; that ambiguity remains explicit. Original chemical_properties={\"cas_rn\":\n    \"56-95-1\", \"data_source\": \"CultureBotHT compounds_to_cas.csv\", \"inchi\": \"InChI=1S/C22H30Cl2N10.2C2H4O2/c23-15-5-9-17(10-6-15)31-21(27)33-19(25)29-13-3-1-2-4-14-30-20(26)34-22(28)32-18-11-7-16(24)8-12-18;2*1-2(3)4/h5-12H,1-4,13-14H2,(H5,25,27,29,31,33)(H5,26,28,30,32,34);2*1H3,(H,3,4)\",\n    \"molecular_formula\": \"C22H30Cl2N10.2C2H4O2\", \"retrieval_date\": \"2026-04-29T06:34:31.158938+00:00\",\n    \"smiles\": \"CC(=O)O.CC(=O)O.N=C(NCCCCCCNC(=N)NC(=N)Nc1ccc(Cl)cc1)NC(=N)Nc1ccc(Cl)cc1\"}.\n    Preserved identifier, ontology mapping and grade, roles, synonyms, counts, status\n    and original history. No mapping, role or release approval. Exact preimage and\n    evidence: reports/hydrate_stock_chemistry_871_268_20261102/source-evidence.json;\n    owner=data/ingredients/mapped/Chlorhexidine_Diacetate_Salt_Hydrate.yaml; before_sha256=3c7a19294fe9b1e9f5197639a7d9f00e3a10ddd755fe5e3be95a52c8bcc42304.'\n  previous_status: MAPPED\n  new_status: MAPPED\n  llm_assisted: true\n  llm_model: gpt-6\n- timestamp: '2026-11-03T06:07:03.766598+00:00'\n  curator: claude\n  action: CORRECTED\n  changes: 'Step 7d (#901; #1117 where applicable): applied only the reviewed field\n    changes [{\"op\":\"set\",\"path\":[\"ontology_mapping\",\"mapping_quality\"],\"before\":\"CLOSE_MATCH\",\"after\":\"NARROW_MATCH\"},{\"op\":\"remove\",\"path\":[\"chemical_properties\",\"cas_rn\"],\"before\":\"56-95-1\",\"after\":null},{\"op\":\"set\",\"path\":[\"supplied_form\"],\"before\":null,\"after\":[{\"name\":\"Chlorhexidine\n    diacetate salt hydrate\",\"cas_rn\":\"206986-79-0\",\"form\":\"diacetate salt hydrate\n    (xH2O; unspecified water stoichiometry)\",\"supplier\":\"Sigma-Aldrich\",\"catalog_number\":\"C6143\",\"notes\":\"CultureBotHT\n    historical compounds_to_cas.csv associated C6143 with CAS56-95-1; the inspected\n    current C6143 supplier page instead lists CAS206986-79-0 and xH2O. Preserve this\n    source-history disagreement. These are procurement cross-references, not an exact\n    CAS identity or fixed-hydration decision for the local hydrate owner; no purchased\n    lot is asserted.\"}]},{\"op\":\"set\",\"path\":[\"synonyms\",0,\"synonym_type\"],\"before\":\"EXACT_SYNONYM\",\"after\":\"REJECTED_LABEL\"}].\n    Original values are preserved here and in the immutable source preimages. Appended\n    scoped mapping evidence. NARROW_MATCH serializes skos:broadMatch; CAS_RN_LOOKUP\n    on the form-specific NCIt identity serializes skos:exactMatch. Preserved prior\n    history, roles, status and occurrence counts; no owner merge or new scientific\n    approval. Review: reports/step7d_mapping_901_20261103/authors/science-a/; primary\n    captures: reports/step7d_mapping_901_20261103/evidence-manifest.json.'\n  previous_status: MAPPED\n  new_status: MAPPED\n  llm_assisted: true\n  llm_model: gpt-6\nchemical_properties:\n  data_source: CultureBotHT compounds_to_cas.csv\n  retrieval_date: '2026-04-29T06:34:31.158938+00:00'\ningredient_type: SINGLE_INGREDIENT\nsupplied_form:\n- name: Chlorhexidine diacetate salt hydrate\n  cas_rn: 206986-79-0\n  form: diacetate salt hydrate (xH2O; unspecified water stoichiometry)\n  supplier: Sigma-Aldrich\n  catalog_number: C6143\n  notes: CultureBotHT historical compounds_to_cas.csv associated C6143 with CAS56-95-1;\n    the inspected current C6143 supplier page instead lists CAS206986-79-0 and xH2O.\n    Preserve this source-history disagreement. These are procurement cross-references,\n    not an exact CAS identity or fixed-hydration decision for the local hydrate owner;\n    no purchased lot is asserted.\n"
  },
