    "raw_text": "identifier: kgmicrobe.ingredient:glucose_acetate\npreferred_term: Glucose + Acetate\nsynonyms:\n- synonym_text: Glucose + Acetate\n  synonym_type: RAW_TEXT\n  source: microbedecoder\nmapping_status: MAPPED\noccurrence_statistics:\n  total_occurrences: 0\n  media_count: 0\n  source_occurrences:\n  - source: microbedecoder\n    count: 3\n    source_columns: bergey:substrates\ncuration_history:\n- timestamp: '2026-08-04T02:54:09.684805+00:00'\n  curator: audit_import_ingredients[microbedecoder]\n  action: CREATED_AS_UNMAPPED\n  changes: Imported from microbedecoder (source_id=kgmicrobe.compound:glucose_acetate);\n    no CAS-RN or CHEBI/NCIT match. Curator review needed.\n  new_status: UNMAPPED\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-08-05T00:01:30.894952+00:00'\n  curator: microbedecoder-residual-dispositions\n  action: FLAGGED_NEEDS_EXPERT\n  changes: 'Not a single-compound grounding target: multi-component blend or named\n    medium; no single ontology term grounds it -- needs decomposition into constituents.'\n  previous_status: UNMAPPED\n  new_status: NEEDS_EXPERT\n  llm_assisted: true\n- timestamp: '2026-08-06T00:00:00+00:00'\n  curator: edison_literature_identity\n  action: ANNOTATED\n  changes: 'Edison LITERATURE (PaperQA3) identity research; report at research/ingredients/Glucose_Acetate-edison-literature.md\n    (local artifact \u2014 research/ is gitignored, so the findings are quoted here rather\n    than linked). Report verdict: ## Curation recommendation \u2014 ### Status CURIEs discussed:\n    CHEBI:17234, CHEBI:17634, CHEBI:30089, CHEBI:15366. Recorded as provenance only\n    \u2014 no grounding applied from this run. Edison''s recommendations are deliberately\n    conservative, and a plausible identifier promoted by a mechanism that never decided\n    anything is what #203 and #263 exist to undo. Any CURIE above is a curator''s\n    to accept or reject.'\n  llm_assisted: true\n- timestamp: '2026-08-14T00:00:00+00:00'\n  curator: decompose_substrate_combinations\n  action: DECOMPOSED_TO_COMPONENTS\n  previous_status: NEEDS_EXPERT\n  new_status: MAPPED\n  changes: 'UNMAPPED_0702 -> kgmicrobe.ingredient:glucose_acetate (FALLBACK_REGISTRY).\n    The label enumerates its own constituents, so this is a decomposition rather than\n    a mapping: no ontology has a term for ''Glucose + Acetate'', and none could \u2014\n    a combination is not a substance. Minted under the #288 STOCK_SOLUTION convention\n    and split on ''+'', which transcribes the label rather than inferring anything.\n    2 of 2 constituents resolve to existing MIM records via docs/data/label_index.csv.\n    ingredient_type=DEFINED_MEDIUM because every constituent is a defined chemical\n    (an unresolved name here means MIM lacks the record, not that the substance is\n    undefined). No concentrations are recorded: the label states none.'\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-08-14T00:00:00+00:00'\n  curator: apply_curated_decompositions\n  action: REPLACED_COMPONENTS_WITH_CURATED\n  changes: 'components replaced with the curated research decomposition, superseding\n    the label split. Components taken from the curated microbedecoder research decomposition\n    (mappings/microbedecoder_residual_research_decomposition.tsv, strategy=split):\n    the label names its constituents. 2 constituent(s), 2 carrying an identifier.\n    That file was produced by the research pass and never written into the records;\n    this applies it. It resolves constituents a label split cannot \u2014 abbreviations\n    such as PY, and named media such as BHI, state no composition to split on. ingredient_type=DEFINED_MEDIUM.\n    No concentrations are recorded: the curated row states none.'\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-08-15T00:00:00+00:00'\n  curator: move_mapped_out_of_unmapped_collection\n  action: MOVED_TO_MAPPED_COLLECTION\n  changes: Moved from unmapped_ingredients.yaml to mapped_ingredients.yaml (#370).\n    The record was already MAPPED; it had been promoted in place by a path that does\n    not move between collections, and reconcile_sssom reads only the mapped collection\n    \u2014 so its mapping was curated but unpublished.\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-08-24T00:00:00+00:00'\n  curator: migrate_component_partonomy\n  action: TYPED_COMPONENT_PARTONOMY\n  changes: '#369: added method/evidence/completeness and explicit reference scope\n    to 2 existing component(s) (MIM_CATALOG); constituent names, identifiers, and\n    concentrations were not changed.'\n  llm_assisted: false\nnotes: Imported from microbedecoder (source_id=kgmicrobe.compound:glucose_acetate);\n  no CAS-RN or CHEBI/NCIT match. Curator review needed.\ningredient_type: NAMED_MEDIUM\ncomponents:\n- component_name: glucose\n  component_id: CHEBI:17234\n  reference_scope: MIM_CATALOG\n  source: microbedecoder research decomposition (#213/#308)\n- component_name: acetate\n  component_id: CHEBI:30089\n  reference_scope: MIM_CATALOG\n  source: microbedecoder research decomposition (#213/#308)\ncomponent_assertion:\n  method: LABEL_ENUMERATION\n  completeness: COMPLETE\n  evidence:\n  - evidence_type: SOURCE_LABEL\n    source: microbedecoder\n    source_record: Glucose + Acetate\n    notes: The source label explicitly names every retained top-level part.\n  - evidence_type: CURATED_DATASET\n    source: mappings/microbedecoder_residual_research_decomposition.tsv\n    source_record: Glucose + Acetate\n    notes: 'Reviewed row: strategy=split, confidence=high; Two carbon substrates.'\n  notes: This is an ingredient/mixture has-part assertion, not an identity mapping,\n    variant hierarchy, or complete culturing recipe.\nontology_mapping:\n  ontology_id: kgmicrobe.ingredient:glucose_acetate\n  ontology_label: Glucose + Acetate\n  ontology_source: kgmicrobe.ingredient\n  mapping_quality: FALLBACK_REGISTRY\n  evidence:\n  - evidence_type: MANUAL_CURATION\n    source: MIM curation (#213/#308)\n    notes: 'The label enumerates its own constituents, so this is a decomposition\n      rather than a mapping: no ontology has a term for ''Glucose + Acetate'', and\n      none could \u2014 a combination is not a substance. Minted under the #288 STOCK_SOLUTION\n      convention and split on ''+'', which transcribes the label rather than inferring\n      anything. 2 of 2 constituents resolve to existing MIM records via docs/data/label_index.csv.\n      ingredient_type=DEFINED_MEDIUM because every constituent is a defined chemical\n      (an unresolved name here means MIM lacks the record, not that the substance\n      is undefined). No concentrations are recorded: the label states none.'\n"
