  "data/ingredients/mapped/Betaine_X_H2o.yaml": {
    "sha256": "30e8e68f84a2fb6e866ce4356a4514f21701286b04a0f70847d6bf9cb2a0320f",
    "raw_text": "identifier: CHEBI:91242\npreferred_term: Betaine x H2O\nontology_mapping:\n  ontology_id: CHEBI:91242\n  ontology_label: glycine betaine hydrate\n  ontology_source: CHEBI\n  mapping_quality: EXACT_MATCH\n  evidence:\n  - evidence_type: DATABASE_MATCH\n    source: CultureMech\n    notes: '[HISTORICAL \u2014 superseded by the #321 re-grade below: this record is a\n      hydrate of CHEBI:17750, not an exact match to it] Imported from CultureMech\n      pipeline, quality=DIRECT_MATCH'\n  - evidence_type: DATABASE_MATCH\n    source: MIM curation (#321/#334)\n    notes: identifier CHEBI:17750 -> kgmicrobe.compound:betaine_x_h2o; mapping_quality\n      EXACT_MATCH -> NARROW_MATCH. The record is a hydrate of CHEBI:17750 ('glycine\n      betaine') and was sharing that term's identifier \u2014 the identity collapse MAPPING_SEMANTICS\n      \u00a73 forbids, which made a distinct substance indistinguishable from its anhydrous\n      parent downstream. ChEBI has no term for this hydrate and the record carries\n      no verified CAS, so steps 1 and 2 are unavailable and step 3 applies.\n  - evidence_type: DATABASE_MATCH\n    source: MIM curation (#321)\n    notes: molecular_formula 'C5H11NO2' -> 'C5H11NO2.H2O'. The recorded value described\n      the anhydrous salt while the label names a hydrate, understating the mass by\n      18 g/mol per water. Corrected because the label states 1 water(s) of hydration,\n      and the recorded formula was byte-identical to the anhydrous parent CHEBI:17750's\n      ChEBI formula ('C5H11NO2') \u2014 the mark of a value inherited from the parent rather\n      than measured for this record. Water appended in ChEBI's own dot-separated notation.\n  - evidence_type: DATABASE_MATCH\n    source: MIM curation (#342)\n    notes: 'mapping_quality NARROW_MATCH -> CLOSE_MATCH, predicate skos:narrowMatch\n      -> skos:closeMatch. narrowMatch asserts this record is *narrower in meaning*\n      than CHEBI:17750 (''glycine betaine'') \u2014 a subsumption ChEBI itself denies:\n      it files hydrates under CHEBI:35505 ''hydrate'', never under the anhydrous compound,\n      which is not an ancestor even transitively. A hydrate is a distinct substance\n      containing the anhydrous form, not a specialization of it. closeMatch claims\n      similarity without subsumption. The ontology_id and the record''s own identifier\n      are unchanged.'\n  - evidence_type: DATABASE_MATCH\n    source: MIM curation (#321)\n    notes: Promoted from CHEBI:17750 ('glycine betaine') to the exact ChEBI hydrate\n      term CHEBI:91242 ('glycine betaine hydrate'). The label names a hydrate and\n      ChEBI has a term for that hydrate, so MAPPING_SEMANTICS.md Section 3 step 1\n      applies.\nsynonyms:\n- synonym_text: 'Role: Growth factor; Properties: Defined component, Simple component,\n    Organic compound'\n  synonym_type: RAW_TEXT\n  source: CultureMech\n- synonym_text: 'Role: Growth factor; Properties: Organic compound, Defined component,\n    Simple component'\n  synonym_type: RAW_TEXT\n  source: CultureMech\n- synonym_text: (trimethylazaniumyl)acetate--water (1/1)\n  synonym_type: EXACT_SYNONYM\n  source: chebi_synonym_review\n- synonym_text: carboxy-N,N,N-trimethylmethanaminium hydroxide\n  synonym_type: EXACT_SYNONYM\n  source: chebi_synonym_review\nmapping_status: MAPPED\noccurrence_statistics:\n  total_occurrences: 40\n  media_count: 40\ncuration_history:\n- timestamp: '2026-03-09T06:54:18.022301+00:00'\n  curator: import_from_culturemech\n  action: IMPORTED\n  changes: Initial import from CultureMech pipeline\n  new_status: MAPPED\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-04-05T19:51:12.210182+00:00'\n  curator: fetch_cas_rn_from_pubchem\n  action: ADDED_CAS_RN\n  changes: Added CAS-RN:107-43-7 from PubChem API via name lookup (Betaine)\n  new_status: MAPPED\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-04-05T23:43:18.984887+00:00'\n  curator: fetch_cas_rn_with_preprocessing\n  action: ADDED_CAS_RN\n  changes: Added CAS-RN:17146-86-0 from PubChem API (preprocessed) via name preprocessing\n    (Betaine x H2O)\n  new_status: MAPPED\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-04-18T00:00:00+00:00'\n  curator: cbclaw_kg_microbe_sweep\n  action: ADDED_SYNONYMS\n  changes: 'Added 14 synonyms from kg-microbe P4.4 enrichment: (trimethylammonio)acetate,\n    (trimethylammoniumyl)acetate, 1-carboxy-N,N,N-trimethylmethanaminium inner salt,\n    2-N,N,N-trimethylammonio acetate, Bet, ... (9 more)'\n  new_status: MAPPED\n  llm_assisted: true\n- timestamp: '2026-04-19T07:39:40.088622+00:00'\n  curator: audit_mim_merge\n  action: MERGED_FROM_DUPLICATES\n  changes: 'Absorbed 1 duplicate MIM record(s) into this one: Betaine.yaml. Synonyms,\n    curation_history, and occurrence counts were unioned/summed; winner selected by\n    highest occurrence count with preferred_term readability tie-break.'\n  new_status: MAPPED\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-04-19T07:39:40.088267+00:00'\n  curator: audit_resolve_risky_cas_rn\n  action: RESOLVED_CAS_RN_CONFLICT\n  changes: 'CAS-RN conflict across merged group (107-43-7|17146-86-0) resolved via\n    OAK canonical xref: 107-43-7 (match)'\n  new_status: MAPPED\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-05-01T07:35:32.404072+00:00'\n  curator: auto_classify_ingredient_type\n  action: AUTO_CLASSIFY_INGREDIENT_TYPE\n  changes: set ingredient_type=SINGLE_INGREDIENT (CHEBI primary)\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-05-01T08:08:28.215517+00:00'\n  curator: auto_classify_ingredient_type\n  action: AUTO_BACKFILL_CHEBI_CHEMISTRY\n  changes: molecular_formula=C5H11NO2; inchi=InChI=1S/C5H11NO2/c1-6(2,3)4-5(7)8/h4H2,1-3H3;\n    smiles=C[N+](C)(C)CC(=O)[O-]\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-05-02T03:12:12.815638+00:00'\n  curator: auto_classify_ingredient_type\n  action: AUTO_CLASSIFY_INGREDIENT_TYPE\n  changes: set ingredient_type=SINGLE_INGREDIENT (chemical structure populated (molecular_formula))\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-06-09T05:23:46.730447+00:00'\n  curator: correct_stale_ontology_labels.py\n  action: CORRECTED\n  changes: 'ontology_label ''Betaine x H2O'' -> ''glycine betaine'': synced to canonical\n    CHEBI label (preferred_term ''Betaine x H2O'' unchanged).'\n- timestamp: '2026-08-13T00:00:00+00:00'\n  curator: mint_hydrate_registry_terms\n  action: MINTED_REGISTRY_FOR_HYDRATE\n  changes: identifier CHEBI:17750 -> kgmicrobe.compound:betaine_x_h2o; mapping_quality\n    EXACT_MATCH -> NARROW_MATCH (#321/#334); \u00a73 step 3.\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-08-13T00:00:00+00:00'\n  curator: add_water_of_hydration\n  action: ADDED_WATER_OF_HYDRATION\n  changes: molecular_formula 'C5H11NO2' -> 'C5H11NO2.H2O' (#321); the label states\n    1 water(s) of hydration, and the recorded formula was byte-identical to the anhydrous\n    parent CHEBI:17750's ChEBI formula ('C5H11NO2') \u2014 the mark of a value inherited\n    from the parent rather than measured for this record. Water appended in ChEBI's\n    own dot-separated notation.\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-08-13T00:00:00+00:00'\n  curator: regrade_hydrate_to_close_match\n  action: REGRADED_HYDRATE_TO_CLOSE_MATCH\n  changes: mapping_quality NARROW_MATCH -> CLOSE_MATCH (#342); a hydrate is not subsumed\n    by its anhydrous form, and ChEBI does not model it as such.\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-08-27T03:16:39.518427+00:00'\n  curator: refresh_occurrence_statistics\n  action: CORRECTED\n  changes: 'occurrence_statistics 20/20 -> 40/40 (media_count/total_occurrences),\n    derived from distinct CultureMech recipe ids in the #337 occurrence table. The\n    prior values came from the importer retired in #453, whose media_count counted\n    a list truncated to 50 examples (#449). [source=ingredient_occurrences.tsv culturemech_rev=15a4da5c08\n    rows=194137 distinct_recipes=15257]'\n- timestamp: '2026-09-10T00:00:00+00:00'\n  curator: fix_remaining_hydrate_regroundings\n  action: PROMOTED_TO_SPECIFIC_HYDRATE\n  changes: identifier kgmicrobe.compound:betaine_x_h2o -> CHEBI:91242; ontology_id\n    CHEBI:17750 -> CHEBI:91242; mapping_quality -> EXACT_MATCH. Structure fields were\n    copied from the exact ChEBI hydrate term, 15 stale anhydrous exact synonym(s)\n    were replaced, and stale kg_microbe_node_id values were aligned where present\n    (#321).\n  llm_assisted: false\nchemical_properties:\n  cas_rn: 590-47-6\n  data_source: OAK/CHEBI exact hydrate term CHEBI:91242\n  retrieval_date: '2026-09-10T00:00:00+00:00'\n  molecular_formula: C5H11NO2.H2O\n  inchi: InChI=1S/C5H11NO2.H2O/c1-6(2,3)4-5(7)8;/h4H2,1-3H3;1H2\n  smiles: C[N+](C)(C)CC(=O)[O-].O\nkg_microbe_node_id: CHEBI:91242\ningredient_type: SINGLE_INGREDIENT\n"
