    "raw_text": "identifier: cas:143314-17-4\npreferred_term: 1-ethyl-3-methylimidazolium acetate\nontology_mapping:\n  ontology_id: CHEBI:63895\n  ontology_label: ionic liquid\n  ontology_source: CHEBI\n  mapping_quality: NARROW_MATCH\n  evidence:\n  - evidence_type: DATABASE_MATCH\n    source: CultureBotHT\n    notes: 'Imported from CultureBotHT. CAS-RN 143314-17-4 present, but no CHEBI entry\n      exists (checked OAK CHEBI sqlite + PubChem CID synonyms). FEBA/Hans80 panels:\n      FEBA_stress. Curator can promote to a CHEBI primary if/when CHEBI adds the term.'\n  - evidence_type: DATABASE_MATCH\n    source: CHEBI via OLS (stem-substring)\n    notes: 'SUPERSEDED (#312): Parent class identified via stem-substring; matched_via=''1-ethyl-3-methylimidazolium\n      acetate'''\n  - evidence_type: MANUAL_CURATION\n    source: MIM curation (#312); chebi.db\n    notes: 'parent CHEBI:61326 (''1-ethyl-3-methylimidazolium'') -> CHEBI:63895 (''ionic\n      liquid''). The record is the neutral salt (CAS 143314-17-4, two-fragment SMILES).\n      CHEBI:61326 ''1-ethyl-3-methylimidazolium'' is the bare cation, C6H11N2 charge\n      +1: a component of the salt, not a broader term for it (Section 6). ChEBI has\n      no term for the acetate salt, so the closest broader class is CHEBI:63895 ''ionic\n      liquid'', the parent the sibling record 1-ethyl-3-methylimidazolium_Lysine already\n      uses. cas: identity, NARROW_MATCH grade and both registry rows unchanged (Section\n      3 step 2).'\nsynonyms:\n- synonym_text: 1-ethyl-3-methyl-1H-imidazol-3-ium\n  synonym_type: REJECTED_LABEL\n  source: chebi_synonym_review\n- synonym_text: 1-ethyl-3-methylimidazolium lysine\n  synonym_type: REJECTED_LABEL\n  source: mappings/ingredient_mappings.sssom.tsv\nmapping_status: MAPPED\noccurrence_statistics:\n  total_occurrences: 0\n  media_count: 0\ncuration_history:\n- timestamp: '2026-04-29T06:51:33.117170+00:00'\n  curator: audit_add_remaining_culturebotht\n  action: CREATED_FROM_CAS_FALLBACK\n  changes: Created with cas:143314-17-4 as primary identifier; no CHEBI entry exists\n    for this compound.\n  new_status: MAPPED\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-05-01T07:35:31.659196+00:00'\n  curator: auto_classify_ingredient_type\n  action: AUTO_CLASSIFY_INGREDIENT_TYPE\n  changes: 'set ingredient_type=SINGLE_INGREDIENT (cas: primary (defined chemical))'\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-05-02T02:51:03.001057+00:00'\n  curator: auto_classify_ingredient_type\n  action: AUTO_BACKFILL_PUBCHEM_CHEMISTRY\n  changes: molecular_formula=C8H14N2O2; smiles=CCN1C=C[N+](=C1)C.CC(=O)[O-]; inchi=InChI=1S/C6H11N2.C2H4O2/c1-3-8-5-4-7(2)6-8;1-2(3)4\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-05-02T03:12:11.759811+00:00'\n  curator: auto_classify_ingredient_type\n  action: AUTO_CLASSIFY_INGREDIENT_TYPE\n  changes: set ingredient_type=SINGLE_INGREDIENT (chemical structure populated (molecular_formula))\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-05-02T04:35:53.785633+00:00'\n  curator: backfill_parent_terms\n  action: BACKFILL_PARENT_CHEBI\n  changes: set ontology_mapping parent=CHEBI:61326 (stem-substring)\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-09-11T06:31:23.789310+00:00'\n  curator: fix_salt_ion_identity_overclaims\n  action: REJECTED_ION_SYNONYMS\n  changes: 'Marked cation/other-salt synonym(s) as REJECTED_LABEL so they cannot leak\n    through SSSOM `other`: ''1-ethyl-3-methyl-1H-imidazol-3-ium'', ''1-ethyl-3-methylimidazolium\n    lysine'' (#315).'\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-09-22T23:25:51.013985+00:00'\n  curator: claude\n  action: REGROUNDED_PARENT_TERM\n  changes: 'broadMatch parent CHEBI:61326 (''1-ethyl-3-methylimidazolium'') -> CHEBI:63895\n    (''ionic liquid'') (#312). The record is the neutral salt (CAS 143314-17-4, two-fragment\n    SMILES). CHEBI:61326 ''1-ethyl-3-methylimidazolium'' is the bare cation, C6H11N2\n    charge +1: a component of the salt, not a broader term for it (Section 6). ChEBI\n    has no term for the acetate salt, so the closest broader class is CHEBI:63895\n    ''ionic liquid'', the parent the sibling record 1-ethyl-3-methylimidazolium_Lysine\n    already uses. cas: identity, NARROW_MATCH grade and both registry rows unchanged\n    (Section 3 step 2).'\n  previous_status: MAPPED\n  new_status: MAPPED\n  llm_assisted: true\n  llm_model: claude-fable-5-1\nchemical_properties:\n  cas_rn: 143314-17-4\n  data_source: CultureBotHT compounds_to_cas.csv\n  retrieval_date: '2026-04-29T06:51:33.117170+00:00'\n  molecular_formula: C8H14N2O2\n  smiles: CCN1C=C[N+](=C1)C.CC(=O)[O-]\n  inchi: InChI=1S/C6H11N2.C2H4O2/c1-3-8-5-4-7(2)6-8;1-2(3)4/h4-6H,3H2,1-2H3;1H3,(H,3,4)/q+1;/p-1\n  pubchem_cid: 11658353\ningredient_type: SINGLE_INGREDIENT\ndiscussions:\n- discussion_id: kgscan-7872af433046\n  prompt: 'Knowledge gap for 1-ethyl-3-methylimidazolium acetate: Ionic liquids (ILs)\n    have been used to replace organic solvents, thereby causing challenges for wastewater\n    treatment.'\n  kind: KNOWLEDGE_GAP\n  status: OPEN\n  rationale: 'Surfaced by the Europe PMC literature gap-signal scan (categories: future_work,\n    limitations_barriers, unclear_unknown). Curator review required: set attaches_to,\n    refine the prompt, and weigh the cited evidence.'\n  attaches_to: []\n  evidence:\n  - reference: PMID:41015306\n    supports: NO_EVIDENCE\n    evidence_source: abstract\n    snippet: Ionic liquids (ILs) have been used to replace organic solvents, thereby\n      causing challenges for wastewater treatment.\n    explanation: Gap-signal sentence (limitations_barriers) from the cited abstract.\n  - reference: PMID:40666722\n    supports: NO_EVIDENCE\n    evidence_source: abstract\n    snippet: By focusing on the deconstruction and reassembly of nonedible agro-wastes,\n      these methods address critical challenges such as resource competition, plastic\n      pollution, and greenhouse gas emissions.\n    explanation: Gap-signal sentence (limitations_barriers) from the cited abstract.\n  - reference: PMID:42195639\n    supports: NO_EVIDENCE\n    evidence_source: abstract\n    snippet: These inherent structural complexities present significant challenges\n      for its efficient isolation and precise transformation.\n    explanation: Gap-signal sentence (limitations_barriers) from the cited abstract.\n  - reference: PMID:40649189\n    supports: NO_EVIDENCE\n    evidence_source: abstract\n    snippet: However, challenges related to large-scale production, functionalization,\n      regulatory frameworks, and safety concerns persist, necessitating further research\n      and innovation.\n    explanation: Gap-signal sentence (future_work, limitations_barriers) from the\n      cited abstract.\n  posed_by: kg-microbe-kgscan\n"
  },
