  "data/ingredients/mapped/Edta.yaml": {
    "sha256": "d766e18a220253f5bfa78e734be9b3a7df8b72ad8a7718ac8602a385e3929701",
    "raw_text": "identifier: CHEBI:4735\npreferred_term: EDTA\nontology_mapping:\n  ontology_id: CHEBI:4735\n  ontology_label: ethylenediaminetetraacetic acid\n  ontology_source: CHEBI\n  mapping_quality: SYNONYM_MATCH\n  evidence:\n  - evidence_type: DATABASE_MATCH\n    source: CultureMech\n    notes: Imported from CultureMech pipeline, quality=DIRECT_MATCH\n  - evidence_type: DATABASE_MATCH\n    source: MIM curation (#319/#320)\n    notes: 'identifier/ontology_id CHEBI:64755 (''EDTA(2-)'') -> CHEBI:4735 (''ethylenediaminetetraacetic\n      acid''); mapping_quality -> SYNONYM_MATCH. ChEBI''s live definition of CHEBI:64755\n      is ''a tetracarboxylic acid anion formed by deprotonation of TWO of the four\n      carboxy groups'' \u2014 a specific charge state this record''s label never asserts.\n      Under #319''s rule a specific definition means descend, unlike the ''at least\n      one'' wording that keeps the anion. Absorbed ''EDTA (acid form)'', which held\n      the free-acid term with ZERO occurrences and already carried ''EDTA'' as a synonym.\n      The corpus keeps separate Na2-EDTA records for the salt, so plain ''EDTA'' denoting\n      the free acid is consistent with how the rest of the family is modelled.'\nsynonyms:\n- synonym_text: 'Properties: Defined component, Organic compound, Simple component'\n  synonym_type: RAW_TEXT\n  source: CultureMech\n- synonym_text: 'Properties: Defined component, Simple component, Organic compound'\n  synonym_type: RAW_TEXT\n  source: CultureMech\n- synonym_text: 'Properties: Organic compound, Simple component, Defined component'\n  synonym_type: RAW_TEXT\n  source: CultureMech\n- synonym_text: 'Properties: Simple component, Defined component, Organic compound'\n  synonym_type: RAW_TEXT\n  source: CultureMech\n- synonym_text: 'Properties: Simple component, Organic compound, Defined component'\n  synonym_type: RAW_TEXT\n  source: CultureMech\n- synonym_text: 2,2',2'',2'''-(ethane-1,2-diyldiammonio)tetraacetate\n  synonym_type: EXACT_SYNONYM\n  source: kg_microbe\n- synonym_text: 2,2',2'',2'''-(ethane-1,2-diyldiazaniumyl)tetraacetate\n  synonym_type: EXACT_SYNONYM\n  source: kg_microbe\n- synonym_text: EDTA (acid form)\n  synonym_type: RAW_TEXT\n  source: MERGED_FROM_CHEBI:4735\n- synonym_text: EDTA (chelating agent)\n  synonym_type: RAW_TEXT\n  source: semantic_review_merge\n- synonym_text: EDTA (chelating agent)\n  synonym_type: RAW_TEXT\n  source: communitymech-unmapped\nmapping_status: MAPPED\noccurrence_statistics:\n  total_occurrences: 569\n  media_count: 568\ncuration_history:\n- timestamp: '2026-03-09T06:54:18.022301+00:00'\n  curator: import_from_culturemech\n  action: IMPORTED\n  changes: Initial import from CultureMech pipeline\n  new_status: MAPPED\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-04-05T19:51:59.318028+00:00'\n  curator: fetch_cas_rn_from_pubchem\n  action: ADDED_CAS_RN\n  changes: Added CAS-RN:60-00-4 from PubChem API via name lookup (EDTA)\n  new_status: MAPPED\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-04-18T00:00:00+00:00'\n  curator: cbclaw_kg_microbe_sweep\n  action: ADDED_SYNONYMS\n  changes: 'Added 2 synonyms from kg-microbe P4.4 enrichment: 2,2'',2'''',2''''''-(ethane-1,2-diyldiammonio)tetraacetate,\n    2,2'',2'''',2''''''-(ethane-1,2-diyldiazaniumyl)tetraacetate'\n  new_status: MAPPED\n  llm_assisted: true\n- timestamp: '2026-05-01T07:35:33.417523+00:00'\n  curator: auto_classify_ingredient_type\n  action: AUTO_CLASSIFY_INGREDIENT_TYPE\n  changes: set ingredient_type=SINGLE_INGREDIENT (CHEBI primary)\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-05-01T08:08:29.391714+00:00'\n  curator: auto_classify_ingredient_type\n  action: AUTO_BACKFILL_CHEBI_CHEMISTRY\n  changes: molecular_formula=C10H14N2O8; inchi=InChI=1S/C10H16N2O8/c13-7(14)3-11(4-8(15)16)1-2-12;\n    smiles=O=C([O-])C[NH+](CC[NH+](CC(=O)[O-])CC(=O)[O-])CC(=\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-05-02T03:12:14.219795+00:00'\n  curator: auto_classify_ingredient_type\n  action: AUTO_CLASSIFY_INGREDIENT_TYPE\n  changes: set ingredient_type=SINGLE_INGREDIENT (chemical structure populated (molecular_formula))\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-06-02T07:05:13.388851+00:00'\n  curator: infer_roles_from_name_lists\n  action: ANNOTATED\n  changes: 'Added media role: CHELATOR (confidence: 0.80)'\n- timestamp: '2026-06-09T05:23:46.759866+00:00'\n  curator: correct_stale_ontology_labels.py\n  action: CORRECTED\n  changes: 'ontology_label ''EDTA'' -> ''EDTA(2-)'': synced to canonical CHEBI label\n    (preferred_term ''EDTA'' unchanged).'\n- timestamp: '2026-07-20T00:00:00+00:00'\n  curator: migrate_media_roles_to_facets\n  action: ANNOTATED\n  changes: 'Migrated legacy media_roles to role facets (#128): CHELATOR -> physicochemical_roles.CHELATOR'\n- timestamp: '2026-08-10T00:00:00+00:00'\n  curator: regrade_synonym_matches\n  action: REGRADED_EXACT_TO_SYNONYM\n  changes: mapping_quality EXACT_MATCH -> SYNONYM_MATCH (#317). The record's label\n    does not equal the term's primary label 'EDTA(2-)'; it matches the ChEBI synonym\n    \"2,2',2'',2'''-(ethane-1,2-diyldiammonio)tetraacetate\" on CHEBI:64755. The schema\n    defines EXACT_MATCH as a direct match to the term and SYNONYM_MATCH as a match\n    to a known synonym, so the recorded grade overstated. ontology_id is unchanged\n    \u2014 the term is correct. The SSSOM predicate is unaffected (both grades emit skos:exactMatch).\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-08-13T00:00:00+00:00'\n  curator: reground_edta_thiamine\n  action: MERGED_FROM\n  changes: identifier/ontology_id CHEBI:64755 -> CHEBI:4735; absorbed 'EDTA (acid\n    form)' (0 occurrences). Occurrences 446/50 -> 446/50 (#319/#320).\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-08-27T03:16:39.518790+00:00'\n  curator: refresh_occurrence_statistics\n  action: CORRECTED\n  changes: 'occurrence_statistics 50/446 -> 568/569 (media_count/total_occurrences),\n    derived from distinct CultureMech recipe ids in the #337 occurrence table. The\n    prior values came from the importer retired in #453, whose media_count counted\n    a list truncated to 50 examples (#449). [source=ingredient_occurrences.tsv culturemech_rev=15a4da5c08\n    rows=194137 distinct_recipes=15257]'\n- timestamp: '2026-09-09T00:00:00+00:00'\n  curator: fix_kg_microbe_node_id_drift\n  action: CORRECTED\n  changes: kg_microbe_node_id CHEBI:64755 -> CHEBI:4735 (#554). The compatibility\n    node id lagged a same-prefix identifier correction; the downstream node id must\n    match the curated identifier unless a record intentionally crosses CURIE prefixes.\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-09-21T21:33:25.379198+00:00'\n  curator: mim_semantic_review_20260921\n  action: MERGED_FROM_DUPLICATES\n  changes: 'Absorbed Edta_Chelating_Agent. The source explicitly names EDTA; the parenthetical\n    function does not turn the substance into the generic class of chelators. Synonym\n    dispositions and role evidence retained. Counts recomputed from distinct recipe\n    membership where nonzero. Evidence: https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI:4735'\n  previous_status: MAPPED\n  new_status: MAPPED\n  llm_assisted: true\n  llm_model: gpt-6\nchemical_properties:\n  cas_rn: 60-00-4\n  data_source: PubChem API\n  retrieval_date: '2026-04-05T19:51:59.317982+00:00'\n  molecular_formula: C10H14N2O8\n  inchi: InChI=1S/C10H16N2O8/c13-7(14)3-11(4-8(15)16)1-2-12(5-9(17)18)6-10(19)20/h1-6H2,(H,13,14)(H,15,16)(H,17,18)(H,19,20)/p-2\n  smiles: O=C([O-])C[NH+](CC[NH+](CC(=O)[O-])CC(=O)[O-])CC(=O)[O-]\nkg_microbe_node_id: CHEBI:4735\ningredient_type: SINGLE_INGREDIENT\nphysicochemical_roles:\n- role: CHELATOR\n  confidence: 0.8\n  evidence:\n  - reference_type: COMPUTATIONAL_PREDICTION\n    reference_text: Inferred from curated media-role name pattern\n    curator_note: Provisional role from a curated name-pattern rule; review recommended.\nmerged:\n- NCIT:C360\n"
