  "data/ingredients/mapped/Aspartate.yaml": {
    "sha256": "0fda5bbe5b55faa59692b792882be73020eba0a72b6345301cf836d91627e102",
    "raw_text": "identifier: CHEBI:29995\npreferred_term: Aspartate\nontology_mapping:\n  ontology_id: CHEBI:29995\n  ontology_label: aspartate(2-)\n  ontology_source: CHEBI\n  mapping_quality: SYNONYM_MATCH\n  evidence:\n  - evidence_type: LEXICAL_MATCH\n    source: microbedecoder\n    notes: 'Imported from microbedecoder via ols-label-exact-chebi. source_id=kgmicrobe.trait:aspartate; '\n  - evidence_type: DATABASE_MATCH\n    source: MIM curation (#319)\n    notes: 'Re-grounded CHEBI:132943 -> CHEBI:29995. CHEBI:132943 is the charge-agnostic\n      parent whose children are aspartate(2-) and aspartate(1-), so a bare label sitting\n      on it declines to state a protonation state. The sibling record Glutamate \u2014\n      same amino-acid family, same bare-label form, same import \u2014 is on CHEBI:29987\n      glutamate(2-), and 30 other bare -ate labels in this corpus are likewise on\n      charged terms. Both terms are stereo-agnostic, so no stereochemical claim is\n      added; ''aspartate'' is a ChEBI synonym of CHEBI:29995, so the lexical evidence\n      survives. Counter-argument on record: MAPPING_SEMANTICS \u00a73 step 4 would keep\n      an evidence-free under-specified label on the parent, and Malate (same hierarchy\n      shape) does exactly that \u2014 \u00a73 does not address protonation, which #319 tracks.'\nsynonyms: []\nmapping_status: MAPPED\noccurrence_statistics:\n  total_occurrences: 12\n  media_count: 12\n  source_occurrences:\n  - source: microbedecoder\n    count: 431\n    source_columns: BacDive_Metabolite_utilization\ncuration_history:\n- timestamp: '2026-08-04T02:54:09.684805+00:00'\n  curator: audit_import_ingredients[microbedecoder]\n  action: CREATED_FROM_INGREDIENT_IMPORT\n  changes: 'Imported from microbedecoder via ols-label-exact-chebi. source_id=kgmicrobe.trait:aspartate; '\n  new_status: MAPPED\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-08-04T03:08:34.142678+00:00'\n  curator: microbedecoder-import-review\n  action: FLAGGED_FOR_REVIEW\n  changes: mapping_status MAPPED -> PENDING_REVIEW\n  notes: Auto-grounded by the microbedecoder import via ols-label-exact. Held at PENDING_REVIEW\n    so the mapping does not reach the published SSSOM before a review-ingredients\n    pass. See reports/microbedecoder_auto_mapped_review.tsv.\n  llm_assisted: true\n- timestamp: '2026-08-04T00:00:00+00:00'\n  curator: review-ingredients\n  action: REVIEWED_AND_PROMOTED\n  changes: mapping_status PENDING_REVIEW -> MAPPED\n  previous_status: PENDING_REVIEW\n  new_status: MAPPED\n  notes: 'Reviewed by review-ingredients: id resolves in local OAK adapter and its\n    canonical label exact-matches the record ontology_label (case-insensitive). This\n    does NOT check for homonyms or wrong-sense class-level matches (see #203). Promoted\n    PENDING_REVIEW -> MAPPED.'\n  llm_assisted: true\n- timestamp: '2026-08-10T00:00:00+00:00'\n  curator: reground_aspartate\n  action: REGROUNDED_CHARGE_STATE\n  changes: identifier/ontology_id CHEBI:132943 -> CHEBI:29995; ontology_label 'aspartate'\n    -> 'aspartate(2-)'; mapping_quality -> SYNONYM_MATCH (#319).\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-08-13T00:00:00+00:00'\n  curator: classify_ingredient_type\n  action: AUTO_CLASSIFY_INGREDIENT_TYPE\n  changes: set ingredient_type=SINGLE_INGREDIENT (CHEBI primary with a structural\n    definition) (#323)\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-08-27T03:16:39.520207+00:00'\n  curator: refresh_occurrence_statistics\n  action: CORRECTED\n  changes: 'occurrence_statistics 0/0 -> 12/12 (media_count/total_occurrences), derived\n    from distinct CultureMech recipe ids in the #337 occurrence table. The prior values\n    came from the importer retired in #453, whose media_count counted a list truncated\n    to 50 examples (#449). [source=ingredient_occurrences.tsv culturemech_rev=15a4da5c08\n    rows=194137 distinct_recipes=15257]'\ningredient_type: SINGLE_INGREDIENT\nchemical_properties:\n  molecular_formula: C4H5NO4\n  smiles: NC(CC(=O)[O-])C(=O)[O-]\n  inchi: InChI=1S/C4H7NO4/c5-2(4(8)9)1-3(6)7/h2H,1,5H2,(H,6,7)(H,8,9)/p-2\n  molecular_weight: 131.087\n  data_source: ChEBI+PubChem\n  retrieval_date: '2026-08-13T04:25:25.555967+00:00'\n"
