m matching the one-letter\n    amino-acid code for aspartate. Three fields, three unrelated substances, all artefacts\n    of one split. The aspartate formula, SMILES and limonene CAS are removed rather\n    than carried onto a tombstone, since all three describe substances this record\n    never denoted. Tombstoned REJECTED, SSSOM rows dropped.'\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-08-15T00:00:00+00:00'\n  curator: fix_tombstone_pointers\n  action: REFRESHED_TOMBSTONE_ONTOLOGY_ID\n  changes: 'ontology_id CHEBI:29958 -> CHEBI:75228 (#360). The merge set identifier\n    and status but left ontology_mapping untouched, so this tombstone kept advertising\n    a term it no longer asserts \u2014 anything indexing by ontology_id routed through\n    it. Now agrees with the merge target ''Sodium lactate''. Provenance is unaffected:\n    what the record used to assert is in this history.'\n  llm_assisted: false\nchemical_properties:\n  data_source: CultureBotHT compounds_to_cas.csv\n  retrieval_date: '2026-04-05T21:48:44.974138+00:00'\ningredient_type: SINGLE_INGREDIENT\n"
