    "raw_text": "identifier: kgmicrobe.ingredient:glucose_maltose_cellobiose_starch_glycerol\npreferred_term: Glucose + Maltose + Cellobiose + Starch + Glycerol\nsynonyms:\n- synonym_text: Glucose + Maltose + Cellobiose + Starch + Glycerol\n  synonym_type: RAW_TEXT\n  source: microbedecoder\nmapping_status: MAPPED\noccurrence_statistics:\n  total_occurrences: 0\n  media_count: 0\n  source_occurrences:\n  - source: microbedecoder\n    count: 1\n    source_columns: literature:substrates\ncuration_history:\n- timestamp: '2026-08-04T02:54:09.684805+00:00'\n  curator: audit_import_ingredients[microbedecoder]\n  action: CREATED_AS_UNMAPPED\n  changes: Imported from microbedecoder (source_id=kgmicrobe.compound:glucose_maltose_cellobiose_starch_glycerol);\n    no CAS-RN or CHEBI/NCIT match. Curator review needed.\n  new_status: UNMAPPED\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-08-05T00:01:30.894952+00:00'\n  curator: microbedecoder-residual-dispositions\n  action: FLAGGED_NEEDS_EXPERT\n  changes: 'Not a single-compound grounding target: multi-component blend or named\n    medium; no single ontology term grounds it -- needs decomposition into constituents.'\n  previous_status: UNMAPPED\n  new_status: NEEDS_EXPERT\n  llm_assisted: true\n- timestamp: '2026-08-06T00:00:00+00:00'\n  curator: edison_literature_identity\n  action: ANNOTATED\n  changes: 'Edison LITERATURE (PaperQA3) identity research; report at research/ingredients/Glucose_Maltose_Cellobiose_Starch_Glycerol-edison-literature.md\n    (local artifact \u2014 research/ is gitignored, so the findings are quoted here rather\n    than linked). Report verdict: ## Recommended record updates \u2014 **Recommended status:**\n    retain `UNMAPPED`, preferably with an explicit local non-identity flag such as\n    `NEEDS_DECOMPOSITION` or `COMPOSITE_LABEL`, if the schema permits. `MAPPED` is\n    inappropriate until the imported occurrence is split into its constituent substrate\n    assertions. CURIEs discussed: CHEBI:17234, CHEBI:17306, CHEBI:17057, CHEBI:28017,\n    CHEBI:17754. Recorded as provenance only \u2014 no grounding applied from this run.\n    Edison''s recommendations are deliberately conservative, and a plausible identifier\n    promoted by a mechanism that never decided anything is what #203 and #263 exist\n    to undo. Any CURIE above is a curator''s to accept or reject.'\n  llm_assisted: true\n- timestamp: '2026-08-14T00:00:00+00:00'\n  curator: decompose_substrate_combinations\n  action: DECOMPOSED_TO_COMPONENTS\n  previous_status: NEEDS_EXPERT\n  new_status: MAPPED\n  changes: 'UNMAPPED_0752 -> kgmicrobe.ingredient:glucose_maltose_cellobiose_starch_glycerol\n    (FALLBACK_REGISTRY). The label enumerates its own constituents, so this is a decomposition\n    rather than a mapping: no ontology has a term for ''Glucose + Maltose + Cellobiose\n    + Starch + Glycerol'', and none could \u2014 a combination is not a substance. Minted\n    under the #288 STOCK_SOLUTION convention and split on ''+'', which transcribes\n    the label rather than inferring anything. 5 of 5 constituents resolve to existing\n    MIM records via docs/data/label_index.csv. ingredient_type=DEFINED_MEDIUM because\n    every constituent is a defined chemical (an unresolved name here means MIM lacks\n    the record, not that the substance is undefined). No concentrations are recorded:\n    the label states none.'\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-08-15T00:00:00+00:00'\n  curator: move_mapped_out_of_unmapped_collection\n  action: MOVED_TO_MAPPED_COLLECTION\n  changes: Moved from unmapped_ingredients.yaml to mapped_ingredients.yaml (#370).\n    The record was already MAPPED; it had been promoted in place by a path that does\n    not move between collections, and reconcile_sssom reads only the mapped collection\n    \u2014 so its mapping was curated but unpublished.\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-08-24T00:00:00+00:00'\n  curator: migrate_component_partonomy\n  action: TYPED_COMPONENT_PARTONOMY\n  changes: '#369: added method/evidence/completeness and explicit reference scope\n    to 5 existing component(s) (MIM_CATALOG); constituent names, identifiers, and\n    concentrations were not changed.'\n  llm_assisted: false\nnotes: Imported from microbedecoder (source_id=kgmicrobe.compound:glucose_maltose_cellobiose_starch_glycerol);\n  no CAS-RN or CHEBI/NCIT match. Curator review needed.\ningredient_type: NAMED_MEDIUM\ncomponents:\n- component_name: Glucose\n  source: MIM label decomposition (#213/#308)\n  component_id: CHEBI:17234\n  reference_scope: MIM_CATALOG\n- component_name: Maltose\n  source: MIM label decomposition (#213/#308)\n  component_id: CHEBI:17306\n  reference_scope: MIM_CATALOG\n- component_name: Cellobiose\n  source: MIM label decomposition (#213/#308)\n  component_id: CHEBI:17057\n  reference_scope: MIM_CATALOG\n- component_name: Starch\n  source: MIM label decomposition (#213/#308)\n  component_id: CHEBI:28017\n  reference_scope: MIM_CATALOG\n- component_name: Glycerol\n  source: MIM label decomposition (#213/#308)\n  component_id: CHEBI:17754\n  reference_scope: MIM_CATALOG\ncomponent_assertion:\n  method: LABEL_ENUMERATION\n  completeness: COMPLETE\n  evidence:\n  - evidence_type: SOURCE_LABEL\n    source: microbedecoder\n    source_record: Glucose + Maltose + Cellobiose + Starch + Glycerol\n    notes: The source label explicitly names every retained top-level part.\n  notes: This is an ingredient/mixture has-part assertion, not an identity mapping,\n    variant hierarchy, or complete culturing recipe.\nontology_mapping:\n  ontology_id: kgmicrobe.ingredient:glucose_maltose_cellobiose_starch_glycerol\n  ontology_label: Glucose + Maltose + Cellobiose + Starch + Glycerol\n  ontology_source: kgmicrobe.ingredient\n  mapping_quality: FALLBACK_REGISTRY\n  evidence:\n  - evidence_type: MANUAL_CURATION\n    source: MIM curation (#213/#308)\n    notes: 'The label enumerates its own constituents, so this is a decomposition\n      rather than a mapping: no ontology has a term for ''Glucose + Maltose + Cellobiose\n      + Starch + Glycerol'', and none could \u2014 a combination is not a substance. Minted\n      under the #288 STOCK_SOLUTION convention and split on ''+'', which transcribes\n      the label rather than inferring anything. 5 of 5 constituents resolve to existing\n      MIM records via docs/data/label_index.csv. ingredient_type=DEFINED_MEDIUM because\n      every constituent is a defined chemical (an unresolved name here means MIM lacks\n      the record, not that the substance is undefined). No concentrations are recorded:\n      the label states none.'\n"
