  "data/ingredients/mapped/Cobalamine.yaml": {
    "sha256": "429d7aa526ebf5588de49fa68239a830b7e029c65f19efcf2ae75aa102e935f0",
    "raw_text": "identifier: CHEBI:30411\npreferred_term: Cobalamine\nontology_mapping:\n  ontology_id: CHEBI:30411\n  ontology_label: cobalamin\n  ontology_source: CHEBI\n  mapping_quality: EXACT_MATCH\n  evidence:\n  - evidence_type: DATABASE_MATCH\n    source: CultureMech\n    notes: Imported from CultureMech pipeline, quality=DIRECT_MATCH\n  - evidence_type: DATABASE_MATCH\n    source: MIM curation (#320/#319)\n    notes: 'identifier and ontology_id CHEBI:28911 -> CHEBI:30411. ChEBI''s live definition\n      of CHEBI:28911 is ''A cobalamin in which the central cobalt atom has an oxidation\n      state of +3'' \u2014 it specifies an oxidation state this record''s label does not.\n      ''Cobalamine'' names the vitamer generically, so MAPPING_SEMANTICS \u00a73 step 4\n      gives it the generic term CHEBI:30411 (''cobalamin''), which was unheld. The\n      record''s own CAS 18534-66-2 is registered by ChEBI against cob(I)alamin \u2014 a\n      *third* oxidation state \u2014 which is the #320 conflict that surfaced this and\n      is itself evidence the record was never specific to +3. Definition read from\n      the live EBI OLS4 API, since #319 records that the local ChEBI build lacks definitions\n      for some of these terms.'\n  - evidence_type: DATABASE_MATCH\n    source: MIM curation (#138/#320)\n    notes: 'Cleared cas_rn, molecular_formula, inchi and smiles, and moved kg_microbe_node_id\n      CHEBI:28911 -> CHEBI:30411. Every one of these encoded the +3 oxidation state\n      this record does not assert. The formula/InChI/SMILES were written by AUTO_BACKFILL_CHEBI_CHEMISTRY\n      on 2026-05-01 by copying CHEBI:28911 while the record was mapped there, so they\n      were a transcription of the grounding rather than evidence for it \u2014 the InChI\n      still ended ''/q;+3/p-2''. The cas_rn 18534-66-2 is cob(I)alamin (KEGG C00853,\n      ChEBI:15982, Gmelin 887721), a THIRD oxidation state, and came from a PubChem\n      name lookup \u2014 the mechanism that also put CHES on Beef extract. CHEBI:30411\n      deliberately carries no formula, charge or mass because its oxidation state\n      is unspecified, so a record grounded there must not carry structure fields that\n      fix one. Leaving them would re-seed the same wrong inference on any future automated\n      re-grading. Note the formula does not discriminate oxidation state in any case:\n      ChEBI records the identical C62H88CoN13O14P for cob(II)alamin and cob(III)alamin,\n      which differ only in the charge field.'\nsynonyms:\n- synonym_text: 'Role: Vitamin; Properties: Organic compound, Defined component, Simple\n    component'\n  synonym_type: RAW_TEXT\n  source: CultureMech\n- synonym_text: COBALAMIN\n  synonym_type: EXACT_SYNONYM\n  source: kg_microbe\n- synonym_text: Cbl\n  synonym_type: EXACT_SYNONYM\n  source: kg_microbe\n- synonym_text: Coalpha-[alpha-(5,6-dimethylbenzimidazolyl)]-cobamide\n  synonym_type: EXACT_SYNONYM\n  source: kg_microbe\n- synonym_text: Cob(III)alamin\n  synonym_type: EXACT_SYNONYM\n  source: kg_microbe\n- synonym_text: Cobalamin (B12)\n  synonym_type: EXACT_SYNONYM\n  source: kg_microbe\n- synonym_text: Cobalamin (III)\n  synonym_type: EXACT_SYNONYM\n  source: kg_microbe\n- synonym_text: alpha-(5,6-dimethylbenzimidazolyl)cobamide\n  synonym_type: EXACT_SYNONYM\n  source: kg_microbe\n- synonym_text: cobalamin(III)\n  synonym_type: EXACT_SYNONYM\n  source: kg_microbe\n- synonym_text: Cobalamin (1 \u03bcg/\u03bcL)\n  synonym_type: RAW_TEXT\n  source: culturemech:output/ingredient_occurrences.tsv\n- synonym_text: cobalamin(1+)\n  synonym_type: RAW_TEXT\n  source: sssom_other_backfill\nmapping_status: MAPPED\noccurrence_statistics:\n  total_occurrences: 9\n  media_count: 9\ncuration_history:\n- timestamp: '2026-03-09T06:54:18.022301+00:00'\n  curator: import_from_culturemech\n  action: IMPORTED\n  changes: Initial import from CultureMech pipeline\n  new_status: MAPPED\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-04-05T19:51:30.156848+00:00'\n  curator: fetch_cas_rn_from_pubchem\n  action: ADDED_CAS_RN\n  changes: Added CAS-RN:18534-66-2 from PubChem API via name lookup (Cobalamine)\n  new_status: MAPPED\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-04-18T00:00:00+00:00'\n  curator: cbclaw_kg_microbe_sweep\n  action: ADDED_SYNONYMS\n  changes: 'Added 8 synonyms from kg-microbe P4.4 enrichment: COBALAMIN, Cbl, Coalpha-[alpha-(5,6-dimethylbenzimidazolyl)]-cobamide,\n    Cob(III)alamin, Cobalamin (B12), ... (3 more)'\n  new_status: MAPPED\n  llm_assisted: true\n- timestamp: '2026-05-01T07:35:32.840424+00:00'\n  curator: auto_classify_ingredient_type\n  action: AUTO_CLASSIFY_INGREDIENT_TYPE\n  changes: set ingredient_type=SINGLE_INGREDIENT (CHEBI primary)\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-05-01T08:08:28.699826+00:00'\n  curator: auto_classify_ingredient_type\n  action: AUTO_BACKFILL_CHEBI_CHEMISTRY\n  changes: molecular_formula=C62H88CoN13O14P; inchi=InChI=1S/C62H90N13O14P.Co/c1-29-20-39-40(21-30(29);\n    smiles=[H][C@]12[C@H](CC(N)=O)[C@@]3(C)CCC(=O)NC[C@@H](C)\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-05-02T03:12:13.445363+00:00'\n  curator: auto_classify_ingredient_type\n  action: AUTO_CLASSIFY_INGREDIENT_TYPE\n  changes: set ingredient_type=SINGLE_INGREDIENT (chemical structure populated (molecular_formula))\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-05-29T23:35:36.110516+00:00'\n  curator: extract_roles_from_synonyms\n  action: ANNOTATED\n  changes: 'Added media role: VITAMIN_SOURCE (confidence: 1.00)'\n- timestamp: '2026-07-20T00:00:00+00:00'\n  curator: migrate_media_roles_to_facets\n  action: ANNOTATED\n  changes: 'Migrated legacy media_roles to role facets (#128): VITAMIN_SOURCE -> nutritional_roles.VITAMIN_SOURCE'\n- timestamp: '2026-08-13T00:00:00+00:00'\n  curator: reground_cobalamin\n  action: REGROUNDED_TO_GENERIC_TERM\n  changes: identifier/ontology_id CHEBI:28911 ('cob(III)alamin') -> CHEBI:30411 ('cobalamin')\n    (#320); the term specified oxidation state +3 and the label specifies none. \u00a73\n    step 4.\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-08-13T00:00:00+00:00'\n  curator: cobalamin_residual_cleanup\n  action: CLEARED_CONTRADICTORY_CHEMISTRY\n  changes: 'Cleared cas_rn, molecular_formula, inchi and smiles, and moved kg_microbe_node_id\n    CHEBI:28911 -> CHEBI:30411. Every one of these encoded the +3 oxidation state\n    this record does not assert. The formula/InChI/SMILES were written by AUTO_BACKFILL_CHEBI_CHEMISTRY\n    on 2026-05-01 by copying CHEBI:28911 while the record was mapped there, so they\n    were a transcription of the grounding rather than evidence for it \u2014 the InChI\n    still ended ''/q;+3/p-2''. The cas_rn 18534-66-2 is cob(I)alamin (KEGG C00853,\n    ChEBI:15982, Gmelin 887721), a THIRD oxidation state, and came from a PubChem\n    name lookup \u2014 the mechanism that also put CHES on Beef extract. CHEBI:30411 deliberately\n    carries no formula, charge or mass because its oxidation state is unspecified,\n    so a record grounded there must not carry structure fields that fix one. Leaving\n    them would re-seed the same wrong inference on any future automated re-grading.\n    Note the formula does not discriminate oxidation state in any case: ChEBI records\n    the identical C62H88CoN13O14P for cob(II)alamin and cob(III)alamin, which differ\n    only in the charge field.'\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-08-27T03:16:39.518580+00:00'\n  curator: refresh_occurrence_statistics\n  action: CORRECTED\n  changes: 'occurrence_statistics 3/3 -> 9/9 (media_count/total_occurrences), derived\n    from distinct CultureMech recipe ids in the #337 occurrence table. The prior values\n    came from the importer retired in #453, whose media_count counted a list truncated\n    to 50 examples (#449). [source=ingredient_occurrences.tsv culturemech_rev=15a4da5c08\n    rows=194137 distinct_recipes=15257]'\n- timestamp: '2026-08-31T23:56:54.854807+00:00'\n  curator: claude_culturemech_alias_backfill\n  action: ADDED_SYNONYMS\n  changes: 'Added 1 CultureMech recipe surface form(s) that folded onto this record''s\n    published label but were absent from MIM''s label index, so CultureMech could\n    not resolve them: ''Cobalamin (1 \u03bcg/\u03bcL)'' (x1 CultureMech mentions). Source: culturemech:output/ingredient_occurrences.tsv.'\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-09-02T17:40:44.716277+00:00'\n  curator: claude_sssom_surface_form_backfill\n  action: ADDED_SYNONYMS\n  changes: 'Recovered 1 surface form(s) that the published SSSOM `other` carried but\n    no curated record did, so a rebuild would have dropped them from KGX: ''cobalamin(1+)''.\n    Tokens already present on the kg-microbe ontology node were left out as redundant\n    (#520).'\n  llm_assisted: false\nchemical_properties:\n  data_source: PubChem API\n  retrieval_date: '2026-04-05T19:51:30.156796+00:00'\nkg_microbe_node_id: CHEBI:30411\ningredient_type: SINGLE_INGREDIENT\nnutritional_roles:\n- role: VITAMIN_SOURCE\n  confidence: 1.0\n  evidence:\n  - reference_type: DATABASE_ENTRY\n    reference_text: Imported from CultureMech pipeline\n    curator_note: 'Original role text: Vitamin Source'\n"
